WEBVTT

1
00:01:09,303 --> 00:01:11,506
(DINOSAUR GRUMBLES)

2
00:01:16,678 --> 00:01:18,245
(FISHING LINE WHIZZES)

3
00:01:21,883 --> 00:01:24,484
(MAN HUMMING)

4
00:01:26,353 --> 00:01:29,958
Any minute now. You see,
you can't rush it, baby girl.

5
00:01:29,991 --> 00:01:32,994
The secret to fishing
is patience.

6
00:01:33,027 --> 00:01:35,395
It's been
five hours, Dad.

7
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:37,932
How much more patience
do we need?

8
00:01:37,966 --> 00:01:40,935
Don't ask me.
Ask the fish.
(GROANS)

9
00:01:40,969 --> 00:01:42,070
(YAWNS)

10
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:44,204
What's up, guys?
It's your boy, Dustin.

11
00:01:44,237 --> 00:01:46,173
I'm out on the boat,
and once again,

12
00:01:46,206 --> 00:01:48,843
my dad can't catch
any fish.

13
00:01:48,876 --> 00:01:50,545
Hey! I heard that.

14
00:01:50,578 --> 00:01:53,615
Don't worry, sweetheart,
I caught these this morning.

15
00:01:53,648 --> 00:01:55,282
At the grocery store.

16
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:58,820
Mom, I'm live!
So embarrassing!

17
00:01:59,621 --> 00:02:01,121
(MEOWS)

18
00:02:04,692 --> 00:02:05,727
(MEOWS)

19
00:02:06,861 --> 00:02:07,929
(YOWLS)

20
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:10,531
(MEOWS)
MOM: Mr. Fluffy Butt, no!

21
00:02:10,565 --> 00:02:11,532
Bad kitty!

22
00:02:13,901 --> 00:02:15,168
Whoa.

23
00:02:15,202 --> 00:02:16,203
Uh... Dad?

24
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,237
(GASPS)
Dad!

25
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:20,173
Shh! Quiet.
You'll scare the fishies.

26
00:02:20,207 --> 00:02:22,376
The boat's on fire!

27
00:02:22,409 --> 00:02:23,276
(YELPS)

28
00:02:23,945 --> 00:02:25,013
(GIRL AND MOM SCREAMS)

29
00:02:25,046 --> 00:02:27,447
(ALL SCREAMING)

30
00:02:31,886 --> 00:02:34,388
Down! Ready... set.

31
00:02:34,789 --> 00:02:35,690
Ruff!

32
00:02:35,723 --> 00:02:36,824
(PUPS PANTING)

33
00:02:36,858 --> 00:02:38,826
Skye! Skye, I'm open!

34
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,360
Marshall, go long!

35
00:02:41,829 --> 00:02:44,431
I got it. I got it. I-- Whoa!

36
00:02:44,464 --> 00:02:46,199
(GRUNTING)

37
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:48,636
Oof!
(PUPS GIGGLE)

38
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:50,404
ALL: Marshall!

39
00:02:50,437 --> 00:02:52,205
I'm okay!
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

40
00:02:52,239 --> 00:02:54,809
Pass is incomplete.
Flag on the play.

41
00:02:54,842 --> 00:02:56,544
Ten yards for clumsiness.

42
00:02:56,577 --> 00:02:57,879
(PUPS LAUGH)

43
00:02:59,246 --> 00:03:01,082
(BEEPS, CRACKLES)

44
00:03:01,115 --> 00:03:02,984
DAD: (OVER RADIO)
<i>Mayday, mayday! S.O.S.!</i>

45
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,318
<i>Our cat set our boat on fire!</i>

46
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:06,688
This is the PAW Patrol.

47
00:03:06,721 --> 00:03:09,423
S.O.S. received.
We're on our way.

48
00:03:10,658 --> 00:03:14,227
(SIREN BLARES)

49
00:03:14,261 --> 00:03:16,931
Come on, pups.
Ryder needs us.

50
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:24,371
That was my first touchdown!
It's still gonna count, right?

51
00:03:24,939 --> 00:03:26,373
Hey, wait up!

52
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:28,375
RYDER: <i>All right, pups.</i>
(BEEPS)

53
00:03:28,408 --> 00:03:30,078
<i>We've got</i>
<i>a five-alarm boat fire</i>

54
00:03:30,111 --> 00:03:31,846
<i>and there are people onboard.</i>

55
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:36,283
<i>Zuma, you are go for launch.</i>

56
00:03:36,316 --> 00:03:37,885
Aye-aye, Ryder, sir!

57
00:03:38,553 --> 00:03:39,554
(BEEPS)

58
00:03:40,253 --> 00:03:41,556
(WHOOSHES)

59
00:03:42,056 --> 00:03:44,525
(HOWLS)

60
00:03:45,927 --> 00:03:48,596
(FANS WHIR)

61
00:03:48,629 --> 00:03:51,699
RYDER: <i>Skye, let's get eyes</i>
<i>on that boat ASAP.</i>

62
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:52,967
I'm on it.

63
00:03:56,204 --> 00:03:59,574
Marshall, Chase, Rubble,
let's fight that fire.

64
00:04:04,178 --> 00:04:05,580
Hoses on!

65
00:04:08,983 --> 00:04:10,785
Help! Up here!
Help!

66
00:04:10,818 --> 00:04:12,153
We're up here!

67
00:04:12,186 --> 00:04:15,489
My name's Zuma
and I'll be your rescue pup.

68
00:04:16,124 --> 00:04:17,225
(SLIDE SQUEAKS)

69
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,327
All right!
Oh, thank goodness.

70
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:23,396
It's time for you dudes
to ride the slide.

71
00:04:24,699 --> 00:04:26,134
Whoo-hoo!

72
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:27,502
Whoa!

73
00:04:28,202 --> 00:04:29,537
Oh! (GIGGLES)

74
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:30,738
(MOM LAUGHS)

75
00:04:31,906 --> 00:04:32,907
Whoo!

76
00:04:34,142 --> 00:04:36,577
RYDER: <i>All right, pups,</i>
<i>it's showtime!</i>

77
00:04:37,178 --> 00:04:39,514
(PUPS HOWL)

78
00:04:40,148 --> 00:04:42,550
Man, this video is fire!

79
00:04:42,583 --> 00:04:45,720
Dustin, get off your phone
and evacuate.

80
00:04:45,753 --> 00:04:48,656
Oh. Gotta go.
Like and subscribe.

81
00:04:48,689 --> 00:04:50,792
Hup! Whoo-hoo!

82
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:52,260
(CLICKS TONGUE)

83
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,326
That's everyone.
(BEEPS)

84
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,662
Whoo-hoo!

85
00:04:54,695 --> 00:04:56,664
RYDER: <i>Nice work, Zuma.</i>
(GASPS)

86
00:04:56,697 --> 00:04:59,267
The cat!
Hey, where's Mr. Fluffy Butt?

87
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,903
He must still be onboard.
(PARENTS GASP)

88
00:05:01,936 --> 00:05:04,972
Mr. Fluffy Butt!

89
00:05:05,006 --> 00:05:07,241
Pups, we've got a cat onboard.

90
00:05:07,275 --> 00:05:09,243
It's always a cat.

91
00:05:09,277 --> 00:05:11,378
Stuck in a tree,
stuck in a boat...

92
00:05:11,411 --> 00:05:13,380
Don't worry. I'm on it.

93
00:05:14,582 --> 00:05:15,482
(GRUNTS)

94
00:05:18,085 --> 00:05:18,986
(WHOOSHES)

95
00:05:20,788 --> 00:05:21,789
(HELMET BEEPS, WHIRS)

96
00:05:27,862 --> 00:05:31,464
Okay, Marshall.
No clumsiness, no mistakes.

97
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:33,501
(STAIR CREAKS)

98
00:05:39,406 --> 00:05:43,077
(SING-SONGY) Here, kitty,
kitty, kitty! Hello!

99
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:45,112
Mr. Fluffy Butt!

100
00:05:45,146 --> 00:05:47,882
Kitty, where are you?

101
00:05:49,717 --> 00:05:50,685
(GASPS)

102
00:05:52,119 --> 00:05:52,987
(GRUNTS)

103
00:05:53,386 --> 00:05:54,454
(GRUNTS)

104
00:05:57,124 --> 00:06:00,127
Looks like we're gonna have
to do this the hard way.

105
00:06:00,161 --> 00:06:01,562
Fire axes!

106
00:06:02,663 --> 00:06:04,031
(GRUNTING)

107
00:06:06,734 --> 00:06:07,668
(MEOWS)

108
00:06:08,135 --> 00:06:09,503
I found the kitty.

109
00:06:09,537 --> 00:06:12,940
He's actually pretty cute.
For a cat.

110
00:06:14,842 --> 00:06:16,077
(GASPS)

111
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:17,812
RYDER: (OVER RADIO) <i>Marshall,</i>
<i>your exit is blocked.</i>

112
00:06:17,845 --> 00:06:20,014
<i>You're gonna have to find</i>
<i>another way out.</i>

113
00:06:20,047 --> 00:06:20,982
Copy that.

114
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,154
Sorry about this, kitty.

115
00:06:27,188 --> 00:06:28,189
(YOWLS)

116
00:06:28,222 --> 00:06:29,389
(MARSHALL GRUNTS)

117
00:06:31,826 --> 00:06:33,060
(MUFFLED YOWL)

118
00:06:34,262 --> 00:06:35,395
(ALL GASP)

119
00:06:35,863 --> 00:06:36,831
(ALL EXHALE)

120
00:06:37,198 --> 00:06:38,431
MOM: Oh, no!

121
00:06:38,465 --> 00:06:39,901
DAD: Come on, man.

122
00:06:39,934 --> 00:06:41,002
Where are they?

123
00:06:41,035 --> 00:06:42,469
No...
Oh, no.

124
00:06:43,337 --> 00:06:44,872
(MARSHALL GASPS)
(ALL CHEER)

125
00:06:44,906 --> 00:06:46,173
Yeah!

126
00:06:46,207 --> 00:06:48,843
That wasn't so bad,
was it, kitty?

127
00:06:48,876 --> 00:06:51,411
(YOWLS WEAKLY)

128
00:06:51,444 --> 00:06:54,081
Come to mommy.
Come to mommy.

129
00:06:54,115 --> 00:06:57,518
Oh, my baby. Mwah.

130
00:06:57,551 --> 00:07:00,354
Ugh. Are you sure
that's Mr. Fluffy Butt?

131
00:07:00,388 --> 00:07:01,789
(MR. FLUFFY BUTT GROWLS)

132
00:07:01,822 --> 00:07:03,024
Don't worry.

133
00:07:03,057 --> 00:07:06,060
His butt will fluff up again
as soon as he dries off.

134
00:07:07,628 --> 00:07:11,265
Loop, swoop, and pull.
(CHUCKLES)

135
00:07:11,299 --> 00:07:13,868
All right,
the hitch is hooked!

136
00:07:13,901 --> 00:07:14,969
Don't worry, kids.

137
00:07:15,002 --> 00:07:17,505
Captain Turbot is the O.G.
of the high seas.

138
00:07:17,538 --> 00:07:19,640
He'll have us back
to land in no time.

139
00:07:19,674 --> 00:07:21,309
You know it!
(FOGHORN BLARES)

140
00:07:21,342 --> 00:07:23,144
Goodbye, Cap'n Turbot!
Goodbye!

141
00:07:23,177 --> 00:07:24,545
Farewell, friends!
Bye!

142
00:07:24,578 --> 00:07:27,014
See you later!
Stay cool,
little doggies!

143
00:07:27,048 --> 00:07:28,549
Bye, Mr. Fluffy Butt!

144
00:07:28,582 --> 00:07:32,086
Nice work, Marshall.
That was a perfect rescue.

145
00:07:32,119 --> 00:07:33,220
What can I say?

146
00:07:33,254 --> 00:07:35,790
Rescue pups
don't make mistakes.

147
00:07:36,857 --> 00:07:39,760
(ALERT BEEPING)

148
00:07:39,794 --> 00:07:42,296
Looks like we're heading
into some weather.

149
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:43,764
Buckle up, pups.

150
00:07:44,332 --> 00:07:47,501
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

151
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,941
PUPS: Whoa!

152
00:07:53,975 --> 00:07:55,676
Whoa!

153
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,945
Isn't this fun?
(GAGS)

154
00:07:57,979 --> 00:08:01,782
(GROANS) I think
I'm more of a land mammal.

155
00:08:09,223 --> 00:08:10,858
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

156
00:08:13,127 --> 00:08:14,996
Switch on the fog lights!

157
00:08:15,029 --> 00:08:16,797
Switching on fog lights.

158
00:08:20,234 --> 00:08:21,702
(THUNDER CRASHES, RUMBLES)

159
00:08:26,374 --> 00:08:27,441
(ALARM BEEPING)
Ryder,

160
00:08:27,475 --> 00:08:29,176
we're drifting off course.
(RYDER GROANS)

161
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:32,813
I'm flying blind out here!
The instruments
are going crazy.

162
00:08:32,847 --> 00:08:35,149
(WEAKLY) That's comforting.

163
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:37,551
Wait, what is that?

164
00:08:38,052 --> 00:08:39,553
What on earth?

165
00:08:42,089 --> 00:08:44,091
Oh, no. No. No, no, no!

166
00:08:45,126 --> 00:08:46,394
Brace for impact!

167
00:08:46,427 --> 00:08:47,828
(PUPS YELP)

168
00:08:51,499 --> 00:08:53,300
Whoa!
(ALL GRUNT)

169
00:09:08,517 --> 00:09:09,583
Ugh.

170
00:09:09,617 --> 00:09:11,118
(PUPS GROAN)

171
00:09:11,152 --> 00:09:12,386
Ugh.

172
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:13,287
(RYDER GRUNTS)

173
00:09:14,188 --> 00:09:15,556
(GROANS)

174
00:09:24,098 --> 00:09:28,469
This doesn't make any sense.
There's no island on the map.

175
00:09:28,503 --> 00:09:30,805
I guess it's time
to update the map.

176
00:09:31,739 --> 00:09:34,008
So what do
we do now?

177
00:09:34,041 --> 00:09:36,577
We've got
to explore the island.

178
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:37,711
Marshall's
right.

179
00:09:37,745 --> 00:09:39,680
But if we're going
into that jungle,

180
00:09:39,713 --> 00:09:41,749
we need to suit up
for the job.

181
00:09:43,217 --> 00:09:44,085
<i>All right, pups,</i>

182
00:09:44,118 --> 00:09:46,187
<i>these are</i>
<i>your new survival suits.</i>

183
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:49,490
<i>They've got</i>
<i>everything you need</i>
<i>to stay alive in the jungle.</i>

184
00:09:49,524 --> 00:09:51,292
<i>Protection from the elements.</i>

185
00:09:51,325 --> 00:09:52,660
<i>Safety gear for climbing.</i>

186
00:09:52,693 --> 00:09:54,695
<i>Built-in floatation devices.</i>
(HELMET BEEPS)

187
00:09:54,728 --> 00:09:58,099
<i>Flashlights, compass</i>
<i>and G.P.S.</i>
(COMPASS WHIRS)

188
00:09:58,132 --> 00:10:00,367
<i>Whatever this island</i>
<i>throws at us,</i>

189
00:10:00,401 --> 00:10:01,869
<i>we'll be prepared.</i>

190
00:10:05,606 --> 00:10:07,842
Ready for action,
Ryder, sir!

191
00:10:09,511 --> 00:10:12,246
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

192
00:10:16,083 --> 00:10:18,219
(FROGS CROAKING)

193
00:10:18,986 --> 00:10:21,422
This place
is amazing.

194
00:10:21,455 --> 00:10:23,858
Everything
is so huge.

195
00:10:24,692 --> 00:10:26,193
Let's climb
to the top of that cliff

196
00:10:26,227 --> 00:10:27,728
and get a lay of the land.

197
00:10:28,295 --> 00:10:29,763
(FROGS CROAKING)

198
00:10:33,067 --> 00:10:33,934
(VINE CREAKS)

199
00:10:34,468 --> 00:10:36,370
(PUPS GRUNTING)

200
00:10:36,403 --> 00:10:38,405
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

201
00:10:40,474 --> 00:10:42,544
(PUPS GRUNTING)

202
00:10:42,577 --> 00:10:43,477
Ugh.

203
00:10:43,512 --> 00:10:46,113
Wow. Look at that view!

204
00:10:54,288 --> 00:10:55,557
Dudes.

205
00:10:55,590 --> 00:10:57,191
It's incredible.

206
00:10:57,224 --> 00:11:00,494
And I've got
the best seat
in the house.

207
00:11:00,529 --> 00:11:01,729
(RUMBLE)
Whoa.

208
00:11:01,762 --> 00:11:03,430
(THUDS)
(YELPS)

209
00:11:03,464 --> 00:11:04,533
(YELLS)

210
00:11:04,566 --> 00:11:06,333
(GRUNTS)

211
00:11:08,102 --> 00:11:08,969
(ALL GASP)

212
00:11:09,604 --> 00:11:10,938
I'm okay!

213
00:11:10,971 --> 00:11:13,841
ALL: Marshall! (GIGGLE)

214
00:11:15,976 --> 00:11:17,711
(ALL GASP)
(WHISPERS)
Marshall!

215
00:11:17,745 --> 00:11:20,214
What? I said I'm okay.
It's kind of my thing.

216
00:11:20,247 --> 00:11:22,383
I crash into something,
then I pop back up

217
00:11:22,416 --> 00:11:23,585
and say, "I'm okay!"

218
00:11:23,618 --> 00:11:24,653
People seem to like it.

219
00:11:24,685 --> 00:11:26,655
Marshall, run!

220
00:11:26,687 --> 00:11:27,988
(GASPS, GRUNTS)

221
00:11:29,624 --> 00:11:32,359
What on earth
is that thing?!

222
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:35,129
(ROARS)

223
00:11:35,162 --> 00:11:38,465
(PUPS SCREAM)
(GASPS, SCREAMS)

224
00:11:38,499 --> 00:11:40,401
Come on! Go, go, go!

225
00:11:40,434 --> 00:11:42,236
(MARSHALL YELPING)

226
00:11:43,037 --> 00:11:44,939
(PUPS PANTING)
(MARSHALL GRUNTS)

227
00:11:44,972 --> 00:11:46,541
Run!

228
00:11:46,575 --> 00:11:48,742
(ROARS)
I am running!

229
00:11:48,776 --> 00:11:52,713
I'm a bulldog, this is as fast
as I can go! (PANTS)

230
00:11:52,746 --> 00:11:54,748
Is that a dinosaur?

231
00:11:54,782 --> 00:11:56,651
I thought those things
were extinct!

232
00:11:56,685 --> 00:11:57,652
(ROARS)

233
00:11:57,686 --> 00:11:59,386
(ALL PANTING)

234
00:12:01,956 --> 00:12:03,924
(ROARS)
(SCREAMS, GRUNTS)

235
00:12:04,358 --> 00:12:06,961
(GRUNTING)

236
00:12:07,428 --> 00:12:08,563
(PANTS)

237
00:12:08,597 --> 00:12:10,532
(GROWLS)
Don't eat me! Don't eat me!

238
00:12:10,565 --> 00:12:11,865
Marshall!

239
00:12:11,899 --> 00:12:14,335
(DISTANT GROWL)
(SNORTS)

240
00:12:16,437 --> 00:12:18,372
(ROARS)

241
00:12:19,073 --> 00:12:21,008
(YELLING)

242
00:12:21,742 --> 00:12:22,810
(YELPS)

243
00:12:25,212 --> 00:12:26,080
(GRUNTS)

244
00:12:28,583 --> 00:12:31,185
(GROWLS)
(ROARS)

245
00:12:31,586 --> 00:12:34,121
(ROARS)

246
00:12:34,154 --> 00:12:36,957
Get out of here,
you old cranky pants!

247
00:12:36,991 --> 00:12:38,292
(WHINES)

248
00:12:38,325 --> 00:12:40,828
(GROWLS)
(MOANS)

249
00:12:43,163 --> 00:12:44,532
(GROANS)

250
00:12:44,566 --> 00:12:45,966
(GROWLS SOFTLY)

251
00:12:46,834 --> 00:12:48,637
You woke her up, didn't you?

252
00:12:48,670 --> 00:12:50,672
Wha-- W-What?

253
00:12:50,705 --> 00:12:51,972
Don't take it personally.

254
00:12:52,006 --> 00:12:55,376
That Spinosaurus is always
cranky after her nap.

255
00:12:58,245 --> 00:13:00,749
Boy, is it good to see
some other pups!

256
