<i>♪ No destination</i>
<i>But it's worth a shot</i>

492
00:23:27,541 --> 00:23:29,176
<i>♪ You gotta let me go</i>

493
00:23:29,210 --> 00:23:30,678
<i>♪ You gotta let me go</i>

494
00:23:31,579 --> 00:23:34,414
All right, team,
we've got 65 million years

495
00:23:34,447 --> 00:23:37,018
of scientific discovery
to catch up on.

496
00:23:37,051 --> 00:23:38,786
Let's get to work.

497
00:23:48,162 --> 00:23:49,530
<i>♪ You gotta let me go</i>

498
00:23:49,563 --> 00:23:51,065
<i>♪ You gotta let me go</i>

499
00:23:51,098 --> 00:23:52,499
<i>♪ You gotta let me go</i>

500
00:23:52,533 --> 00:23:53,701
(GRUNTS)
<i>♪ Ready for war</i>

501
00:23:53,734 --> 00:23:54,669
<i>♪ Got my armor gear</i>
<i>Sharpen your sword</i>

502
00:23:54,702 --> 00:23:55,770
<i>♪ 'Cause the time is near</i>

503
00:23:55,803 --> 00:23:57,271
<i>♪ Gotta do it big</i>
<i>Like Bon Iver</i>

504
00:23:57,305 --> 00:23:58,873
<i>♪ I'm a rock star</i>
<i>On a chandelier</i>

505
00:23:58,906 --> 00:24:00,641
<i>♪ Off the walls, yeah</i>
<i>I'm about to go crazy</i>

506
00:24:00,675 --> 00:24:02,076
<i>♪ Free the beast, ain't nobody</i>
<i>That could tame me</i>

507
00:24:02,109 --> 00:24:03,644
<i>♪ What a thrill</i>
<i>Always seems to amaze me</i>

508
00:24:03,678 --> 00:24:05,379
<i>♪ In the forest with the youth</i>
<i>And they're raving</i>

509
00:24:05,413 --> 00:24:06,681
<i>♪ Dancin' nonstop</i>
<i>'Til the break of dawn</i>

510
00:24:06,714 --> 00:24:07,982
<i>♪ Sheriffs come around</i>
<i>Probably best to run</i>

511
00:24:08,015 --> 00:24:09,817
<i>♪ Fire in my eyes</i>
<i>Can't catch me now</i>

512
00:24:09,850 --> 00:24:11,484
<i>♪ I'm young and numb</i>
<i>Trying to have some fun</i>

513
00:24:11,519 --> 00:24:12,720
<i>♪ Don't judge me</i>

514
00:24:12,753 --> 00:24:13,888
<i>♪ You only live once</i>
<i>Homies in the back</i>

515
00:24:13,921 --> 00:24:15,589
<i>♪ So we gotta live it up</i>
Say "ah."

516
00:24:16,390 --> 00:24:18,893
(ROARS)
(SCREAMS)

517
00:24:20,995 --> 00:24:22,596
<i>♪ Running miles</i>
<i>And running wild</i>

518
00:24:22,630 --> 00:24:23,731
<i>♪ I'm chugging</i>
<i>Like I'm fueling</i>

519
00:24:23,764 --> 00:24:24,899
(SIGHS)
<i>♪ Houston</i>

520
00:24:24,932 --> 00:24:26,434
<i>♪ And tellin' 'em</i>
<i>That I'm comin' up</i>

521
00:24:26,466 --> 00:24:27,467
<i>♪ I'm cruisin'</i>
Huh?

522
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:28,669
<i>♪ Space boost comin' loose</i>

523
00:24:28,703 --> 00:24:29,637
(CHITTERS)
<i>♪ But all I feel</i>

524
00:24:29,670 --> 00:24:30,671
<i>♪ Is music like</i>
(GASPS)

525
00:24:30,705 --> 00:24:31,973
<i>♪ Nah, nah, nah, nah</i>

526
00:24:32,006 --> 00:24:33,607
(CHITTERING)
<i>♪ Never look back</i>

527
00:24:33,641 --> 00:24:35,242
<i>♪ Nah, nah, nah, nah</i>

528
00:24:35,276 --> 00:24:36,711
<i>♪ Never look back</i>

529
00:24:36,744 --> 00:24:38,412
<i>♪ Never look back</i>

530
00:24:38,446 --> 00:24:39,814
<i>♪ Run wild</i>

531
00:24:39,847 --> 00:24:42,283
<i>♪ I'm on a mission</i>
<i>And I won't stop</i>

532
00:24:42,316 --> 00:24:43,451
(BLOWS RASPBERRY)

533
00:24:43,483 --> 00:24:45,987
<i>♪ No destination</i>
<i>But it's worth a shot</i>

534
00:24:46,620 --> 00:24:48,155
<i>♪ You gotta let me go</i>

535
00:24:48,189 --> 00:24:49,623
<i>♪ You gotta let me go</i>

536
00:24:49,657 --> 00:24:51,491
<i>♪ You gotta let me go ♪</i>

537
00:24:53,361 --> 00:24:55,329
Uh, Rex, we're out of water.

538
00:24:55,363 --> 00:24:57,698
Ugh, the water wheel's
jammed again.

539
00:24:57,732 --> 00:25:00,534
Sometimes stuff
from the river
gets stuck in it.

540
00:25:03,070 --> 00:25:05,973
(CREAKING, SLOSHING)

541
00:25:12,947 --> 00:25:14,648
(GRUNTING)

542
00:25:20,154 --> 00:25:21,255
There we go.

543
00:25:22,056 --> 00:25:22,923
Ouch!

544
00:25:24,458 --> 00:25:25,693
(CREATURE TRILLS)

545
00:25:26,794 --> 00:25:28,796
(CHITTERS)

546
00:25:28,829 --> 00:25:31,132
Did you just
throw this stick at me?

547
00:25:33,234 --> 00:25:34,935
Hey, come back here!

548
00:25:39,540 --> 00:25:41,742
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

549
00:25:43,512 --> 00:25:44,912
(CREATURE SNORTS)
(YELPS)

550
00:25:45,913 --> 00:25:47,281
(SCREECHES)

551
00:25:47,314 --> 00:25:48,616
Oh. (CHUCKLES)

552
00:25:48,649 --> 00:25:49,750
(SIGHS, CHUCKLES)

553
00:25:49,784 --> 00:25:52,386
That's not much
of a roar for a T-Rex.

554
00:25:52,420 --> 00:25:53,287
(TRILLS)

555
00:25:55,289 --> 00:25:56,257
(CHITTERS)

556
00:25:56,290 --> 00:25:57,191
Oh,

557
00:25:57,224 --> 00:25:58,793
I see what's going on here.

558
00:25:58,826 --> 00:26:00,494
You want to play fetch.

559
00:26:00,529 --> 00:26:02,596
(SQUAWKS)
Why didn't you say so?

560
00:26:02,630 --> 00:26:06,167
You're talking to
the original fetch master.

561
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,301
(GRUNTS)

562
00:26:07,334 --> 00:26:08,736
(GRUNTS)
(PANTS)

563
00:26:11,939 --> 00:26:13,274
(MURMURS)

564
00:26:13,307 --> 00:26:15,042
Okay. One more throw.

565
00:26:15,076 --> 00:26:17,512
But then I got to get
back to work. Deal?

566
00:26:17,546 --> 00:26:18,746
(SQUEAKS)

567
00:26:20,147 --> 00:26:21,048
(GRUNTS)

568
00:26:21,615 --> 00:26:23,884
(CHITTERS)

569
00:26:25,186 --> 00:26:26,887
(GRUNTS)

570
00:26:27,421 --> 00:26:28,389
No!

571
00:26:28,422 --> 00:26:30,424
(WHIMPERS, YELPS)

572
00:26:30,458 --> 00:26:32,726
(SCREAMS)
Hang on, I'm coming!

573
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:35,362
(WHIMPERS, SQUEALS)

574
00:26:36,531 --> 00:26:38,466
(PANTING)

575
00:26:38,499 --> 00:26:40,535
(GRUNTS)
(FRIGHTENED SQUEALING)

576
00:26:40,569 --> 00:26:42,571
(GRUNTS, PANTS)

577
00:26:42,603 --> 00:26:44,338
(SQUAWKING)

578
00:26:46,006 --> 00:26:47,208
(YELPS)

579
00:26:47,975 --> 00:26:50,077
I'm right behind you!
(WHINES)

580
00:26:50,111 --> 00:26:51,879
It's gonna be okay!

581
00:26:53,147 --> 00:26:54,381
Grab on!
(WHIMPERING)

582
00:26:56,450 --> 00:26:57,952
(MARSHALL GRUNTS)

583
00:27:02,223 --> 00:27:06,327
Oh, no.
Please be a little one,
please be a little one.

584
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:07,795
(T-REX SQUEAKS)

585
00:27:09,830 --> 00:27:13,033
It's not a little one!

586
00:27:13,067 --> 00:27:16,103
(BOTH SCREAMING)

587
00:27:23,612 --> 00:27:24,812
(GASPS)

588
00:27:25,279 --> 00:27:27,047
(GASPS) I got you!

589
00:27:27,081 --> 00:27:27,982
(GRUNTS)

590
00:27:29,216 --> 00:27:31,218
(MARSHALL PANTING)

591
00:27:39,426 --> 00:27:40,861
You okay?

592
00:27:42,363 --> 00:27:44,165
(TRILLS EAGERLY)

593
00:27:44,198 --> 00:27:47,668
(CHUCKLES) I think that's
enough fetch for one day.

594
00:27:48,369 --> 00:27:50,404
(ENGINE CLANKING)

595
00:27:50,437 --> 00:27:53,307
(FOGHORN BLARES)

596
00:28:01,516 --> 00:28:06,220
Dino Island has the biggest
diamond deposit in the world.

597
00:28:06,253 --> 00:28:07,721
And the two of you

598
00:28:07,755 --> 00:28:10,625
are going
to help me get it.

599
00:28:10,659 --> 00:28:13,528
Phase one of the plan
is led by Harper Cutlass,

600
00:28:13,562 --> 00:28:15,296
our expert survival guide.

601
00:28:15,329 --> 00:28:17,431
You're here to help us
get through the jungle

602
00:28:17,464 --> 00:28:22,870
and make sure
we don't get eaten by any
of those nasty dinosaurs.

603
00:28:22,903 --> 00:28:25,773
Don't worry.
I'm a master of stealth.

604
00:28:25,806 --> 00:28:28,976
Those dinosaurs
will never hear us coming.

605
00:28:29,009 --> 00:28:30,077
(YELPS)

606
00:28:30,110 --> 00:28:31,345
(KITTIES YOWL)

607
00:28:33,080 --> 00:28:35,182
Everything's fine!
Nothing to worry about.

608
00:28:36,083 --> 00:28:37,985
Okay.

609
00:28:38,018 --> 00:28:41,355
Phase two of our plan
is where you come into play.

610
00:28:41,388 --> 00:28:45,459
Alistair Stonewall.
Mining and explosives expert.

611
00:28:45,492 --> 00:28:49,330
There's nothing
I can't dig.
Nothing I can't drill.

612
00:28:49,363 --> 00:28:50,464
And if all else fails,

613
00:28:50,497 --> 00:28:54,068
there's nothing
I can't blast
to smithereens! (LAUGHS)

614
00:28:54,101 --> 00:28:57,071
(NERVOUS CHUCKLE)
Uh, love the enthusiasm.

615
00:28:57,104 --> 00:28:59,907
But let's save it
for the diamonds, shall we?

616
00:29:00,307 --> 00:29:02,276
Land ho!

617
00:29:02,309 --> 00:29:03,377
Whoo-hoo!

618
00:29:04,546 --> 00:29:07,047
Ah... There it is.

619
00:29:07,649 --> 00:29:11,185
Dino Island. (CACKLES)

620
00:29:14,088 --> 00:29:16,591
(RUMBLES)

621
00:29:16,625 --> 00:29:19,927
Hey! (CHUCKLES)
(PUPS GIGGLE)

622
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:23,531
That's all of them.
The dinos are squeaky clean.

623
00:29:24,798 --> 00:29:26,735
Marshall! There you are.

624
00:29:26,767 --> 00:29:28,469
We were wondering
where you went.

625
00:29:28,503 --> 00:29:30,204
Uh, you're not gonna
believe this,

626
00:29:30,237 --> 00:29:32,373
but I think
I made a new friend.

627
00:29:32,406 --> 00:29:33,642
(CHITTERS)

628
00:29:33,675 --> 00:29:36,010
(CHUCKLES) He's a little shy.

629
00:29:36,043 --> 00:29:38,879
(GASPS) He's so cute!

630
00:29:38,912 --> 00:29:40,749
I saved him
when he fell
in the river,

631
00:29:40,781 --> 00:29:42,717
and he's been
following me
ever since.

632
00:29:42,751 --> 00:29:45,720
(GASPS) No fair!
I want a dinosaur B.F.F.

633
00:29:45,754 --> 00:29:46,954
(GRUNTS)
(SQUEALS)

634
00:29:46,987 --> 00:29:49,456
It's me and you, buddy.
Best friends forever.

635
00:29:49,490 --> 00:29:51,792
(SCREECHING)
Oh-- Ow! Ow, ow, ow!

636
00:29:51,825 --> 00:29:52,826
Okay, stop, stop, stop!

637
00:29:52,860 --> 00:29:54,361
Never mind!
(HISSES)

638
00:29:54,395 --> 00:29:57,865
(PUPS AND RYDER LAUGH)

639
00:29:57,898 --> 00:30:00,535
So, does
this little guy
have a name?

640
00:30:00,568 --> 00:30:01,802
Not that I know of.

641
00:30:01,835 --> 00:30:03,304
Well, we should
give him one.

642
00:30:03,337 --> 00:30:06,608
It's not every day
you get to name
a dinosaur.

643
00:30:06,641 --> 00:30:07,808
Let's see.

644
00:30:07,841 --> 00:30:10,612
You're bright red
with a white tummy

645
00:30:10,645 --> 00:30:13,280
and a little bit of green
on your tail.

646
00:30:13,314 --> 00:30:15,182
We should call you...

647
00:30:15,215 --> 00:30:16,417
Rhubarb!

648
00:30:16,751 --> 00:30:18,385
Rhubarb?!

649
00:30:19,654 --> 00:30:21,121
I think he likes
his name.

650
00:30:21,155 --> 00:30:22,956
Too late
to change it now.

651
00:30:22,990 --> 00:30:24,759
Well, if he's happy,
I'm happy.

652
00:30:24,793 --> 00:30:26,594
Rhubarb it is!

653
00:30:27,361 --> 00:30:28,495
(GRUNTS)

654
00:30:28,530 --> 00:30:30,397
(SCREECHES)

655
00:30:31,865 --> 00:30:33,568
What was that?

656
00:30:33,601 --> 00:30:36,738
(CHUCKLES)
Rhubarb's still
working on his roar.

657
00:30:36,771 --> 00:30:38,038
(SNICKERS)

658
00:30:46,548 --> 00:30:49,950
(ENGINES PUTTER)

659
00:30:52,286 --> 00:30:53,521
(CREAKS, SQUEALS)

660
00:30:56,624 --> 00:30:58,992
(GASPS) Well, I'll be.

661
00:30:59,026 --> 00:31:00,628
(BRACHIOSAURUS LOWS)

662
00:31:02,664 --> 00:31:05,232
(WHOOPS, LAUGHS)

663
00:31:05,265 --> 00:31:07,401
Look at the size
of that thing.

664
00:31:14,108 --> 00:31:16,009
Ugh, well,
we don't have all day.

665
00:31:16,043 --> 00:31:18,312
Get that thing
out of the way.

666
00:31:18,345 --> 00:31:21,048
Stand back. I got this.
(KNUCKLES CRACK)

667
00:31:21,850 --> 00:31:25,486
(LOWS MOCKINGLY)

668
00:31:25,520 --> 00:31:28,455
(BABBLES)

669
00:31:28,489 --> 00:31:30,825
(TRILLS, CHITTERS)

670
00:31:30,859 --> 00:31:32,359
What are you doing?

671
00:31:32,393 --> 00:31:36,564
That is my dinosaur call.
I'm trying to get
his attention.

672
00:31:36,598 --> 00:31:38,999
Aw, isn't that cute?

673
00:31:39,032 --> 00:31:41,201
Not gonna work, though.
Out of my way!

674
00:31:41,235 --> 00:31:43,937
(YELPS)
Coming through! (GRUNTS)

675
00:31:43,971 --> 00:31:46,907
(GRUNTS, LOWS)

676
00:31:46,940 --> 00:31:48,510
What do you think
you're doing?

677
00:31:48,543 --> 00:31:52,379
I'm not letting
this Cretaceous cretin
stand in my way.

678
00:31:52,413 --> 00:31:54,181
(MEWS)
(HORN HONKS)

679
00:31:56,383 --> 00:31:58,018
(YELPS)
(MEOWS)

680
00:31:58,520 --> 00:31:59,420
(MEOWS)

681
00:31:59,453 --> 00:32:00,487
Move it!

682
00:32:00,522 --> 00:32:03,424
Get out of my way,
I've got places to be!

683
00:32:03,457 --> 00:32:05,025
Scoot! Shoo! Vamoose!

684
00:32:06,895 --> 00:32:08,295
(ROARS)

685
00:32:10,565 --> 00:32:13,000
(BRACHIOSAURUS GROANS)

686
00:32:19,306 --> 00:32:21,308
(ROARS)

687
00:32:24,344 --> 00:32:25,345
Whoa.

688
00:32:25,379 --> 00:32:28,917
What?! That wasn't my fault.
He tripped on his own.

689
00:32:28,949 --> 00:32:30,585
You saw it, right, kitties?

690
00:32:30,618 --> 00:32:31,985
(KITTIES MEW)

691
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:42,597
(WAILS DEEPLY)

692
00:32:44,498 --> 00:32:45,432
Okay, Rhubarb,

693
00:32:45,466 --> 00:32:47,869
we've got to work
on that roar of yours.

694
00:32:47,902 --> 00:32:49,169
You're a T-Rex.

695
00:32:49,203 --> 00:32:51,606
You should have a big, loud,

696
00:32:51,639 --> 00:32:53,641
commanding roar!
(GRUNTS)

697
00:32:53,675 --> 00:32:57,144
Here, do what I do.
Put your feet apart like this.

698
00:32:58,078 --> 00:32:59,848
Now stand up straight.

699
00:32:59,881 --> 00:33:00,882
(MURMURS)

700
00:33:00,915 --> 00:33:02,684
Chest forward.

701
00:33:02,717 --> 00:33:03,651
(GRUNTS)

702
00:33:03,685 --> 00:33:05,820
But keep your tail
in the air.

703
00:33:05,854 --> 00:33:08,322
Take a deep breath.
(INHALES)

704
00:33:08,823 --> 00:33:10,090
(INHALES)

705
00:33:10,123 --> 00:33:12,392
Now... roar! (ROARS)

706
00:33:12,426 --> 00:33:14,529
(ALL ROAR)

707
00:33:14,562 --> 00:33:16,564
(SCREECHES WEAKLY)

708
00:33:19,066 --> 00:33:23,838
Okay, not bad.
It was a good start.

709
00:33:23,872 --> 00:33:27,074
You'll get there.
You just need
to stick with it.

710
00:33:27,107 --> 00:33:29,443
(COMPUTER CHIMES)
(BEEPS)

711
00:33:29,476 --> 00:33:31,411
Hey, Heidi.
How's it going
out there?

712
00:33:31,445 --> 00:33:34,147
<i>Ryder!</i>
<i>There's a Brachiosaurus</i>
<i>in trouble!</i>

713
00:33:34,181 --> 00:33:36,149
(LOWS)
(REX GASPS)

714
00:33:36,985 --> 00:33:38,085
Where are you?

715
00:33:38,118 --> 00:33:39,854
<i>We're on the far side</i>
<i>of the island.</i>

716
00:33:39,888 --> 00:33:41,556
<i>I'm sending you</i>
<i>the coordinates now.</i>

717
00:33:41,589 --> 00:33:43,123
We're on our way.

718
00:33:43,558 --> 00:33:44,424
Come on, pups!

719
00:33:44,458 --> 00:33:47,529
No dino's too big,
no pup's too small.

720
00:33:47,562 --> 00:33:49,564
(ENGINES WHIRRING)

721
00:33:50,832 --> 00:33:52,700
RYDER: <i>Pups,</i>
<i>get ready to launch.</i>

722
00:33:52,734 --> 00:33:53,601
(MACHINERY BEEPS)

723
00:33:55,503 --> 00:33:56,370
(CHIMES)

724
00:33:59,339 --> 00:34:00,575
(HOWLS)

725
00:34:03,878 --> 00:34:05,178
(SCREEN CHIMES)

726
00:34:08,883 --> 00:34:09,784
(SIREN WHOOPS)

727
00:34:16,858 --> 00:34:18,492
(BEEPS)
Ready for launch!

728
00:34:18,526 --> 00:34:19,794
(ENGINE POWERS UP)
RYDER: Marshall, go!

729
00:34:19,827 --> 00:34:21,029
(PING)
(WHOOSHES)

730
00:34:21,061 --> 00:34:23,531
(ENGINE ROARS)

731
00:34:23,565 --> 00:34:25,198
(HOWLS)

732
00:34:27,802 --> 00:34:29,469
(WHIRS, BEEPS)

733
00:34:29,504 --> 00:34:32,105
(HOWLS)

734
00:34:32,139 --> 00:34:33,942
RYDER: Skye, go!
(BEEPS, WHOOSHES)

735
00:34:33,975 --> 00:34:35,577
(ENGINE ROARS)

736
00:34:37,745 --> 00:34:40,113
(ENGINE REVS, BLASTS)

737
00:34:42,884 --> 00:34:44,117
RYDER: Zuma, go!

738
00:34:44,752 --> 00:34:46,588
(ENGINE ROARS)

739
00:34:47,989 --> 00:34:49,489
RYDER: Rocky, go!

740
00:34:49,524 --> 00:34:51,391
(PULSES, WHOOSHES)

741
00:34:51,425 --> 00:34:52,860
RYDER: Rubble, go!
(BEEPS)

742
00:34:54,562 --> 00:34:56,430
(RUBBLE HOWLS)

743
00:34:59,333 --> 00:35:01,468
RYDER: Chase, go!
(BEEPS, WHOOSHES)

744
00:35:01,501 --> 00:35:02,704
(CHASE HOWLS)

745
00:35:04,237 --> 00:35:06,741
(SIREN WAILING)

746
00:35:06,774 --> 00:35:08,810
(PUPS HOWL)

747
00:35:08,843 --> 00:35:10,678
(MARSHALL HOWLS)

748
00:35:11,746 --> 00:35:13,681
(SIREN WAILS)

749
00:35:18,886 --> 00:35:20,722
GENE: Oh, thank goodness
you're here.

750
00:35:21,556 --> 00:35:22,322
What happened?

751
00:35:22,356 --> 00:35:24,559
I don't know.
He must have slipped.

752
00:35:27,829 --> 00:35:29,597
(LOWS SOFTLY)

753
00:35:32,066 --> 00:35:33,801
(WAILS)

754
00:35:34,334 --> 00:35:35,603
We don't have much time!

755
00:35:35,637 --> 00:35:38,271
Chase, Rocky,
let's get him strapped in.

756
00:35:38,305 --> 00:35:39,607
You got it, Ryder!

757
00:35:40,875 --> 00:35:42,543
Dropping in. (GRUNTS)

758
00:35:46,213 --> 00:35:47,849
Let's do this.

759
00:35:48,516 --> 00:35:49,851
(HOWLS)

760
00:35:50,417 --> 00:35:51,919
(HOWLS)

761
00:35:54,589 --> 00:35:56,390
Marshall, I need you
to use your winch

762
00:35:56,423 --> 00:35:58,358
to pull that
Brachiosaurus
out of there.

763
00:35:58,392 --> 00:36:01,228
I'm on it!
Stabilizers down.

764
00:36:04,799 --> 00:36:05,933
Here we go.

765
00:36:10,638 --> 00:36:12,239
(LOWS)

766
00:36:12,272 --> 00:36:14,341
Let's flip and clip.

767
00:36:17,812 --> 00:36:19,547
Deploying net.

768
00:36:25,252 --> 00:36:26,954
MARSHALL:
Here comes the hook!

769
00:36:28,589 --> 00:36:31,125
The Brachiosaurus
is secure.

770
00:36:31,159 --> 00:36:33,493
All right, Marshall,
haul him up.

771
00:36:33,528 --> 00:36:34,862
Copy that.

772
00:36:34,896 --> 00:36:37,431
Okay, Marshall,
no mistakes.

773
00:36:38,231 --> 00:36:39,967
(WINCH WHIRS)

774
00:36:44,138 --> 00:36:46,074
Dino's on the move!

775
00:36:46,107 --> 00:36:48,475
Bringing him up
slow and steady.

776
00:36:56,951 --> 00:36:58,519
(LOWS)

777
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:00,588
(GROANS)
(BEEPING)

778
00:37:00,621 --> 00:37:02,523
Something's stuck
in the winch!

779
00:37:02,557 --> 00:37:04,224
(CREAKING)

780
00:37:04,257 --> 00:37:06,928
Hang on! I'll fix it. (GRUNTS)

781
00:37:07,595 --> 00:37:08,462
(GRUNTS)

782
00:37:09,262 --> 00:37:10,665
(HYDRAULICS HISSING)

783
00:37:13,701 --> 00:37:16,236
No, no. No, no, no, no!
No, no!

784
00:37:17,839 --> 00:37:18,773
Marshall!

785
00:37:18,806 --> 00:37:20,842
(YELPING)

786
00:37:21,374 --> 00:37:22,910
(GROANS, GRUNTS)

787
00:37:24,145 --> 00:37:26,279
(PANTS, GRUNTS)

788
00:37:26,781 --> 00:37:27,749
(GRUNTS)

789
00:37:27,782 --> 00:37:28,683
Look out!

790
00:37:28,716 --> 00:37:29,617
Whoa!

791
00:37:37,992 --> 00:37:39,426
My truck!

792
00:37:43,197 --> 00:37:46,500
(LOWS, RUMBLES)

793
00:37:46,868 --> 00:37:48,169
Oh, no.

794
00:37:48,202 --> 00:37:50,470
How are we gonna get
that dino out now?

795
00:37:52,039 --> 00:37:53,808
What can we do to help?

796
00:37:54,909 --> 00:37:56,911
(TRICERATOPS LOWING)

797
00:37:58,345 --> 00:38:00,447
Everybody, grab a rope!

798
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:02,282
(TRICERATOPS RUMBLES)

799
00:38:02,917 --> 00:38:06,220
(ENGINE REVS)

800
00:38:06,254 --> 00:38:09,690
RYDER: Three, two, one,

801
00:38:09,724 --> 00:38:10,958
pull!

802
00:38:16,998 --> 00:38:20,802
(ENGINES REVVING)
(ALL GRUNTING)

803
00:38:22,970 --> 00:38:24,005
RYDER: It's stuck!

804
00:38:26,073 --> 00:38:27,275
RYDER: Come on!

805
00:38:27,307 --> 00:38:28,709
(ENGINE STRAINS)
(GASPS)

806
00:38:37,852 --> 00:38:39,386
It's working!

807
00:38:45,092 --> 00:38:47,460
(BOTH HOWL)

808
00:38:49,396 --> 00:38:52,733
(RUMBLES, LOWS)

809
00:38:52,767 --> 00:38:54,202
(PUPS CHEER, LAUGH)

810
00:38:54,235 --> 00:38:55,870
Great work, team.

811
00:38:55,903 --> 00:38:57,638
Nicely done,
pups!

812
00:38:57,672 --> 00:39:00,842
(ROARS)

813
00:39:00,875 --> 00:39:03,010
(LOWS)

814
00:39:07,414 --> 00:39:10,350
CHASE: You gotta watch
your step next time, big guy.

815
00:39:13,486 --> 00:39:16,224
He seems so steady
on his feet.

816
00:39:16,257 --> 00:39:18,526
I wonder what made him fall.

817
00:39:24,232 --> 00:39:25,099
(MEOWS)

818
00:39:26,466 --> 00:39:28,669
(HEAVY SNORES)

819
00:39:36,177 --> 00:39:37,111
We're here!

820
00:39:38,045 --> 00:39:39,046
(TIRES SCREECH)

821
00:39:39,080 --> 00:39:40,380
Oh!
(HORN HONKS)

822
00:39:40,413 --> 00:39:41,849
Uh-huh?

823
00:39:47,855 --> 00:39:49,090
Stay behind me.

824
00:39:49,123 --> 00:39:52,760
Who knows
what kind of monsters
are hiding in these shadows.

825
00:39:53,628 --> 00:39:54,996
(TWIG SNAPS)
(GASPS)

826
00:40:00,301 --> 00:40:01,269
(CHIRPS)

827
00:40:01,302 --> 00:40:02,469
(SCREAMS)

828
00:40:03,905 --> 00:40:04,805
(CHITTERS)

829
00:40:04,839 --> 00:40:06,240
(CHUCKLES)

830
00:40:06,274 --> 00:40:08,776
Sorry, I-- I thought
it would be bigger.

831
00:40:08,809 --> 00:40:10,511
(SQUEALS, CHITTERS)
Don't worry.

832
00:40:10,544 --> 00:40:13,347
I'm not gonna tell anybody
you scream like that.

833
00:40:13,381 --> 00:40:17,118
Ooh. Check it out.
This is igneous rock.

834
00:40:17,151 --> 00:40:21,088
The whole island is sitting
on top of a giant volcano!

835
00:40:21,122 --> 00:40:22,657
A volcano.

836
00:40:22,690 --> 00:40:25,226
Not sure I like
the sound of that.

837
00:40:25,259 --> 00:40:26,459
It's nothing
to worry about.

838
00:40:26,493 --> 00:40:29,263
This baby's been dormant
for thousands of years.

839
00:40:29,297 --> 00:40:30,998
It's not waking up
for anybody.

840
00:40:31,032 --> 00:40:35,636
(GASPS) It's even sparklier
than it was on TV!

841
00:40:35,670 --> 00:40:37,437
I'm gonna be rich.
(KITTIES MEW)

842
00:40:37,470 --> 00:40:39,140
No, filthy rich.

843
00:40:39,173 --> 00:40:42,710
No! Filthy, stinking rich!

844
00:40:42,743 --> 00:40:44,145
(CACKLES)

845
00:40:44,178 --> 00:40:45,445
Mm!
(CRUNCHES)

846
00:40:45,478 --> 00:40:46,647
Ow!
(SNARLS)

847
00:40:46,681 --> 00:40:49,617
Get off me! Get off me!
(SQUEAKS, CHITTERS)

848
00:40:49,650 --> 00:40:51,319
Ow!
(DINOSAURS CHITTER)

849
00:40:51,352 --> 00:40:53,087
Don't worry,
I'll set some traps.

850
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:55,823
Teach these bitey little
critters some manners.

851
00:40:55,856 --> 00:40:56,824
(CREAKS, SNAPS)

852
00:40:56,857 --> 00:40:58,125
(YELPS)

853
00:40:58,159 --> 00:40:59,527
Everything's fine.

854
00:41:00,094 --> 00:41:02,530
(CHUCKLES) Okay.

855
00:41:03,496 --> 00:41:05,498
Well, what are we
standing around for?

856
00:41:05,533 --> 00:41:06,867
Let's mine these diamonds

857
00:41:06,901 --> 00:41:09,203
and get out of here
before the PAW Patrol

858
00:41:09,236 --> 00:41:11,105
starts sniffing around.

859
00:41:11,138 --> 00:41:12,239
(CHITTERING)
(YELLS)

860
00:41:12,273 --> 00:41:13,607
(BANG, TWANG)

861
00:41:14,342 --> 00:41:15,710
Ooh. (CHUCKLES)

862
00:41:15,743 --> 00:41:18,245
That's not good.
(DINOSAURS CHITTER)

863
00:41:18,279 --> 00:41:20,314
(CHITTERING LAUGHTER)

864
00:41:20,348 --> 00:41:21,449
(GRUNTS)

865
00:41:21,481 --> 00:41:24,285
We're going to need
a little more power.

866
00:41:24,318 --> 00:41:25,286
(PICK CLANGS)

867
00:41:25,319 --> 00:41:27,154
(ENGINE REVS, SPUTTERS)
(SQUEAL)

868
00:41:27,188 --> 00:41:30,791
Hey, Humdinger!
You sure you
can handle that thing?

869
00:41:30,825 --> 00:41:33,761
(REVVING, SPUTTERING)
What? I can't hear you!

870
00:41:33,794 --> 00:41:36,097
(BABBLES)

871
00:41:38,099 --> 00:41:40,368
(BABBLES, SCREAMS)

872
00:41:40,401 --> 00:41:41,302
(GRUNTS)

873
00:41:41,335 --> 00:41:45,239
(DINOSAURS CACKLE)

874
00:41:46,240 --> 00:41:47,675
Ha, ha, ha.

875
00:41:47,708 --> 00:41:50,011
You little lizards
think this is funny?

876
00:41:50,044 --> 00:41:52,847
I'll give you something
to laugh about.

877
00:41:53,381 --> 00:41:55,683
Assemble the drill!

878
00:41:55,716 --> 00:41:57,985
Now, that's what
I'm talking about.

879
00:41:58,019 --> 00:42:01,489
Let's get this party started!
(LAUGHS)

880
00:42:01,522 --> 00:42:02,923
(GIGGLES)

881
00:42:04,959 --> 00:42:07,561
(BRACHIOSAURUS LOWS)

882
00:42:08,095 --> 00:42:10,097
(SQUEAKING CROW)

883
00:42:21,876 --> 00:42:23,277
(METALLIC THUD)
(YELPS)

884
00:42:27,148 --> 00:42:30,184
You really smashed
that sucker up good,
didn't you?

885
00:42:30,818 --> 00:42:32,053
Yep.

886
00:42:32,086 --> 00:42:35,056
Eh! Don't worry about it.
Mistakes happen.

887
00:42:35,089 --> 00:42:38,292
Rescue pups aren't
supposed to make mistakes.

888
00:42:38,325 --> 00:42:39,827
(METALLIC THUD,
CLATTERING)

889
00:42:41,162 --> 00:42:44,598
That's not true.
Everybody makes mistakes.

890
00:42:45,032 --> 00:42:46,600
Not you.

891
00:42:46,634 --> 00:42:47,768
Are you kidding?

892
00:42:47,802 --> 00:42:50,304
I make more mistakes
than anyone.

893
00:42:51,238 --> 00:42:53,074
You do?

894
00:42:53,107 --> 00:42:56,043
You look up
and see a finished treehouse.

895
00:42:56,077 --> 00:42:57,144
But what you don't see

896
00:42:57,178 --> 00:43:00,147
is all the mistakes
it took to get there.

897
00:43:00,181 --> 00:43:03,284
Making mistakes is how
you learn and get better.

898
00:43:04,051 --> 00:43:05,419
Well, that...

899
00:43:05,453 --> 00:43:07,621
and never giving up.

900
00:43:10,925 --> 00:43:12,293
(STRAINS)

901
00:43:12,326 --> 00:43:14,228
All right, let her rip!

902
00:43:15,396 --> 00:43:17,631
(ENGINE REVS)
(CACKLES)

903
00:43:17,665 --> 00:43:19,834
Hang on, kitties.

904
00:43:19,867 --> 00:43:22,336
(BOTH CHIRP)
(BLADES WHIR)

905
00:43:25,172 --> 00:43:26,340
(HUMDINGER CACKLES)

906
00:43:28,409 --> 00:43:30,878
Whoa! Whoa!

907
00:43:30,911 --> 00:43:32,313
Whoa!

908
00:43:32,346 --> 00:43:33,548
Wow--

909
00:43:33,582 --> 00:43:34,782
(YELPS)

910
00:43:34,815 --> 00:43:37,618
(CRASHING)
(ENGINE SPUTTERS)

911
00:43:38,152 --> 00:43:39,954
(CLANGS, CLATTERING)

912
00:43:41,889 --> 00:43:45,059
What kind of cut-rate
mining equipment
is this?!

913
00:43:45,092 --> 00:43:48,462
Hey, it's not my fault.
The diamond is too hard.

914
00:43:48,496 --> 00:43:50,397
I've never seen
anything like it.

915
00:43:50,431 --> 00:43:51,966
So, what do we do?

916
00:43:52,399 --> 00:43:53,434
When in doubt...

917
00:43:53,467 --> 00:43:56,003
we blast it out!

918
00:43:56,036 --> 00:43:57,171
(GIGGLES)

919
00:43:57,204 --> 00:43:59,707
(SING-SONGY) Blast it out,
blast it out, blast it out!

920
00:43:59,740 --> 00:44:03,578
I said we blast it out,
blast it out, blast it out!

921
00:44:03,612 --> 00:44:04,745
Whoo-hoo!
(CHITTERS)

922
00:44:04,778 --> 00:44:07,248
(FEARFUL SQUEAL)

923
00:44:07,281 --> 00:44:08,949
Everybody stand back.

924
00:44:08,983 --> 00:44:12,219
Oh, oh, oh! Can I press
the dynamite plunger thingy?

925
00:44:12,253 --> 00:44:14,155
Can I? Please?

926
00:44:16,423 --> 00:44:17,725
(SIGHS) Fine.

927
00:44:17,758 --> 00:44:19,860
Just stop making that face.
You're freaking me out!

928
00:44:19,894 --> 00:44:21,795
(GIGGLES)
I've wanted to do this

929
00:44:21,829 --> 00:44:24,431
ever since I started
watching cartoons.

930
00:44:24,465 --> 00:44:27,134
(HUMS <i>SHAVE AND A HAIRCUT)</i>
(CLICKS)

931
00:44:29,069 --> 00:44:32,574
(DISTANT RUMBLE)
(DINOSAURS CHITTER)

932
00:44:32,607 --> 00:44:34,441
(ALL LOWING)

933
00:44:34,475 --> 00:44:37,211
(LOWS)
(GRUNTING)

934
00:44:37,244 --> 00:44:38,779
(SQUEALS)

935
00:44:38,812 --> 00:44:41,482
(DINOSAURS SQUEAL, BELLOW)

936
00:44:41,516 --> 00:44:42,917
(WHOOPS)

937
00:44:42,950 --> 00:44:45,486
I love it
when it goes boom!

938
00:44:45,520 --> 00:44:46,420
(MEOWS)

939
00:44:48,455 --> 00:44:49,823
Ooh.

940
00:44:49,857 --> 00:44:51,125
(CHUCKLES) Wow!

941
00:44:51,158 --> 00:44:55,564
(CACKLES) It worked!
It worked! (LAUGHS)

942
00:44:55,597 --> 00:44:57,865
We're gonna need
more dynamite.

943
00:44:57,898 --> 00:45:00,401
A lot more dynamite.

944
00:45:09,210 --> 00:45:10,477
(TOOL CLANGS)

945
00:45:10,512 --> 00:45:11,912
Huh?
(METALLIC RATTLING)

946
00:45:16,217 --> 00:45:18,419
(DISTANT RUMBLING)

947
00:45:18,452 --> 00:45:19,887
What is that?

948
00:45:19,920 --> 00:45:22,022
Do you guys hear
that sound?

949
00:45:23,224 --> 00:45:24,291
It's my stomach.

950
00:45:24,325 --> 00:45:26,827
Those baby dinosaurs
ate all my pup treats.

951
00:45:26,860 --> 00:45:29,564
(LOW RUMBLE)
(NERVOUS CHUCKLE)

952
00:45:29,598 --> 00:45:31,765
Somebody get
this guy a snack!

953
00:45:31,799 --> 00:45:33,702
(ALL SCREAM)
(DINOSAURS ROAR)

954
00:45:33,734 --> 00:45:34,669
Whoa!

955
00:45:34,703 --> 00:45:35,736
(GASPS)

956
00:45:35,769 --> 00:45:38,072
It's a stampede! (YELPS)
(DINOSAURS ROAR)

957
00:45:38,105 --> 00:45:39,073
BOTH: Whoa!

958
00:45:39,106 --> 00:45:42,276
(MARSHALL WHIMPERS)
(ROCKY YELPING)

959
00:45:46,380 --> 00:45:49,116
(BRACHIOSAURUS LOWS)

960
00:45:50,184 --> 00:45:52,920
They're heading
straight for
the geology camp!

961
00:45:55,456 --> 00:45:57,626
Come on, pups,
let's roll!

962
00:45:57,659 --> 00:46:00,194
(PUPS HOWL)

963
00:46:00,227 --> 00:46:03,464
I can't go on the rescue.
I've got no truck!

964
00:46:04,265 --> 00:46:06,267
(ENGINE REVS)

965
00:46:07,201 --> 00:46:09,436
(ENGINE WHIRS)

966
00:46:13,508 --> 00:46:16,377
(WHOOSHES)
(PUPS HOWL)

967
00:46:19,113 --> 00:46:21,549
(MACHINERY HISSES)
Anybody need a ride?

968
00:46:22,983 --> 00:46:25,286
Come on, Rhubarb,
let's go!

969
00:46:32,594 --> 00:46:33,894
SCIENTIST: Our hypothesis

970
00:46:33,927 --> 00:46:37,364
is that lava tubes running
underneath the dormant volcano

971
00:46:37,398 --> 00:46:38,767
kept the island warm enough

972
00:46:38,799 --> 00:46:42,303
for these dinosaurs
to survive the Ice Age.

973
00:46:42,336 --> 00:46:44,071
CAMERAMAN: And cut!

974
00:46:44,104 --> 00:46:45,607
We got it.

975
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:46,840
(CRUNCHES)
(SCREAMS)

976
00:46:46,874 --> 00:46:47,941
Take cover!

977
00:46:47,975 --> 00:46:49,511
SCIENTIST: Whoa!
(GASPS)

978
00:46:49,544 --> 00:46:51,312
Oh, look out!
(YELPS)

979
00:46:51,345 --> 00:46:54,616
MAN: Help, help!
WOMAN: It's a stampede!

980
00:46:54,649 --> 00:46:55,517
MAN: Whoa!

981
00:46:56,718 --> 00:46:59,053
(GASPS, YELLS)

982
00:46:59,086 --> 00:47:01,855
(STEGOSAURUS GRUNTS)
(SCREAMS)

983
00:47:02,389 --> 00:47:03,758
(GRUNTS, YELPS)

984
00:47:03,792 --> 00:47:05,359
(YELPS, GASPS)

985
00:47:05,392 --> 00:47:07,061
(SCREAMS)

986
00:47:07,861 --> 00:47:09,698
(ENGINE WHOOSHES)

987
00:47:09,731 --> 00:47:12,232
Ryder! Someone's caught
in the stampede!

988
00:47:13,500 --> 00:47:15,436
Copy that.
We're on our way.

989
00:47:17,739 --> 00:47:19,741
(PANTING) There she is!

990
00:47:19,774 --> 00:47:21,543
HEIDI: Help, over here!

991
00:47:21,576 --> 00:47:22,777
Hang on!

992
00:47:22,811 --> 00:47:23,911
I'm going in.

993
00:47:23,944 --> 00:47:25,580
(ENGINE ROARS)

994
00:47:27,114 --> 00:47:30,484
There's too many dinos.
We can't get in there!

995
00:47:30,518 --> 00:47:32,252
Well, who's gonna save her?

996
00:47:33,320 --> 00:47:35,824
Come on, Rhubarb,
it's up to us!

997
00:47:35,889 --> 00:47:36,990
Hi-yah!

998
00:47:38,660 --> 00:47:40,861
(DINOSAURS GRUNTING)

999
00:47:41,563 --> 00:47:42,863
Hi-yah!

1000
00:47:43,531 --> 00:47:45,332
Yeah! Marshall!

1001
00:47:47,868 --> 00:47:51,305
I can see her!
She's just up ahead!

1002
00:47:51,338 --> 00:47:53,974
Marshall,
I'm dropping a rescue line.

1003
00:47:54,007 --> 00:47:55,342
(BEEPS)
(WHIRRING)

1004
00:47:59,179 --> 00:48:02,049
Come on, Rhubarb,
we've got to get in close!

1005
00:48:02,082 --> 00:48:04,719
(YELPS)
I can't hang on!

1006
00:48:04,753 --> 00:48:06,721
Steady, steady.

1007
00:48:06,755 --> 00:48:07,655
Help!

1008
00:48:07,689 --> 00:48:09,123
Now! (GRUNTS)

1009
00:48:10,357 --> 00:48:11,225
(GRUNTS)

1010
00:48:12,192 --> 00:48:14,863
(GASPS, YELPS)
It's gonna be okay!

1011
00:48:14,895 --> 00:48:16,964
(PANTS) I can't
hang on anymore!

1012
00:48:16,997 --> 00:48:20,167
I just need you to hang on
for five more seconds.

1013
00:48:20,200 --> 00:48:21,836
You can let go in five...

1014
00:48:21,870 --> 00:48:22,903
(PANTS)

1015
00:48:22,936 --> 00:48:24,171
...four...

1016
00:48:24,873 --> 00:48:26,641
three...
(YELLS)

1017
00:48:26,674 --> 00:48:27,642
...two...

1018
00:48:28,208 --> 00:48:29,176
(GRUNTS)

1019
00:48:29,778 --> 00:48:31,478
...one!
(SCREAMS)

1020
00:48:31,513 --> 00:48:32,980
(SCREAM FADES)

1021
00:48:33,648 --> 00:48:34,816
(SCREAM GETS LOUDER)

1022
00:48:34,849 --> 00:48:36,350
Yeah!

1023
00:48:36,383 --> 00:48:37,317
(GASPS)

1024
00:48:37,351 --> 00:48:39,621
(WHIMPERS, WHOOPS)

1025
00:48:39,654 --> 00:48:41,155
Did you see that?!

1026
00:48:41,188 --> 00:48:43,323
SKYE: <i>Got her.</i>
<i>Nice moves, Marshall.</i>

1027
00:48:43,357 --> 00:48:45,693
<i>Now get out of there.</i>
(WHISTLES)

1028
00:48:45,727 --> 00:48:46,694
(RHUBARB CHITTERS)

1029
00:48:47,529 --> 00:48:48,395
(TRILLS)

1030
00:48:49,129 --> 00:48:50,832
You ready, buddy?

1031
00:48:50,865 --> 00:48:51,766
(SQUEAKS)

1032
00:48:51,800 --> 00:48:53,267
Let's do this.

1033
00:48:53,300 --> 00:48:54,803
(GRUNTS) Oof!

1034
00:48:54,836 --> 00:48:56,805
(MARSHALL GRUNTING)

1035
00:48:56,838 --> 00:48:58,105
Oof.

1036
00:48:58,138 --> 00:49:00,441
(RHUBARB WHIMPERS)
No! Rhubarb!

1037
00:49:01,108 --> 00:49:03,377
(BRACHIOSAURUS LOWS)

1038
00:49:13,120 --> 00:49:14,589
RYDER: (MUFFLED) Marshall?

1039
00:49:16,490 --> 00:49:17,625
Marshall?

1040
00:49:23,096 --> 00:49:25,767
You took a pretty hard fall
out there.

1041
00:49:25,800 --> 00:49:28,168
The good thing
is nothing's broken.

1042
00:49:29,002 --> 00:49:30,672
Where's Rhubarb?

1043
00:49:32,039 --> 00:49:33,741
We don't know.

1044
00:49:33,775 --> 00:49:35,610
He got lost
in the stampede.

1045
00:49:35,643 --> 00:49:37,010
I have to find him.

1046
00:49:37,044 --> 00:49:40,447
You need to rest.
The team's out
looking for him now.

1047
00:49:41,048 --> 00:49:43,083
Rhubarb could be hurt.

1048
00:49:46,754 --> 00:49:48,489
This is all my fault.

1049
00:49:49,323 --> 00:49:52,292
No, it's not.
It was an accident.

1050
00:49:52,326 --> 00:49:55,496
Accidents seem to happen
a lot around me.

1051
00:49:55,530 --> 00:49:58,165
I used to be funny
being the clumsy pup.

1052
00:49:58,198 --> 00:49:59,934
I'd fall down
and say "I'm okay"

1053
00:49:59,968 --> 00:50:01,936
and everything would be fine.

1054
00:50:01,970 --> 00:50:03,605
But now it's not fine.

1055
00:50:05,005 --> 00:50:07,274
I keep making mistakes.

1056
00:50:07,307 --> 00:50:09,878
I almost got eaten
by a dinosaur.

1057
00:50:09,911 --> 00:50:11,746
I wrecked my truck.

1058
00:50:11,779 --> 00:50:13,648
And this time,
when I messed up,

1059
00:50:14,481 --> 00:50:16,918
I hurt my friend.

1060
00:50:16,951 --> 00:50:19,954
Sometimes I think
you'd all be better off

1061
00:50:19,988 --> 00:50:22,022
without a clumsy pup like me.

1062
00:50:22,055 --> 00:50:23,892
Don't say that.

1063
00:50:23,925 --> 00:50:26,126
You're only focusing
on your mistakes.

1064
00:50:26,159 --> 00:50:28,563
Think of all
the good things
you've done.

1065
00:50:30,397 --> 00:50:32,667
Do you remember
the first time we met?

1066
00:50:37,639 --> 00:50:38,773
(PUPPIES YIP FAINTLY)

1067
00:50:39,741 --> 00:50:40,808
(BARKS, PANTS)

1068
00:50:40,842 --> 00:50:43,210
Welcome to
the PAW Patrol tryouts.

1069
00:50:43,243 --> 00:50:46,146
Good luck out there, pups.
Let's see what you can do.

1070
00:50:46,179 --> 00:50:49,349
(WHISTLE BLOWS)
(PUPPIES BARK)

1071
00:50:54,822 --> 00:50:55,890
(GRUNTS)

1072
00:50:55,924 --> 00:50:57,324
(PUPPY BARKS)
(GRUNTS)

1073
00:50:57,357 --> 00:50:58,893
(GRUNTING)

1074
00:50:58,927 --> 00:51:00,093
Whoa! (GRUNTS)

1075
00:51:02,329 --> 00:51:03,196
(GRUNTS)

1076
00:51:03,798 --> 00:51:05,600
(PANTS)
(PUPPIES BARK)

1077
00:51:06,901 --> 00:51:08,235
(MARSHALL GRUNTS, PANTS)

1078
00:51:08,803 --> 00:51:09,671
(GRUNTS)

1079
00:51:10,538 --> 00:51:11,606
(GRUNTS)

1080
00:51:11,639 --> 00:51:13,440
(GRUNTS) Whoa!

1081
00:51:13,473 --> 00:51:14,509
(PUPPY BARKS)

1082
00:51:14,842 --> 00:51:15,710
Hup.

1083
00:51:16,644 --> 00:51:18,478
Yeah-- Uh-- Uh!
(GRUNTS)

1084
00:51:19,847 --> 00:51:21,114
(PUPPY BARKS, PANTS)

1085
00:51:21,649 --> 00:51:22,817
(MARSHALL GRUNTS)

1086
00:51:23,885 --> 00:51:24,786
Oof.

1087
00:51:25,520 --> 00:51:26,821
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

1088
00:51:36,296 --> 00:51:38,398
(RAIN PATTERING)
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

1089
00:51:39,634 --> 00:51:42,202
Ryder,
come see this.

1090
00:51:52,880 --> 00:51:53,748
(GRUNTS)

1091
00:51:54,281 --> 00:51:55,182
(GRUNTS, PANTS)

1092
00:51:55,215 --> 00:51:56,450
(GRUNTS) Whoa.

1093
00:51:56,483 --> 00:51:57,652
Whoa! (GRUNTS)

1094
00:52:02,056 --> 00:52:04,592
(THUNDER CLAPS)
I can do this.

1095
00:52:05,793 --> 00:52:07,629
(GRUNTING)

1096
00:52:08,896 --> 00:52:10,297
RYDER: <i>I didn't</i>
<i>pick you because</i>

1097
00:52:10,330 --> 00:52:12,132
<i>you never made mistakes.</i>
(MARSHALL GRUNTS)

1098
00:52:12,165 --> 00:52:13,534
(YELPS, YELLS)

1099
00:52:14,769 --> 00:52:17,170
(GRUNTS)

1100
00:52:17,204 --> 00:52:19,239
RYDER: <i>I picked you</i>
<i>because you're the pup</i>

1101
00:52:19,272 --> 00:52:20,908
<i>that never gives up.</i>
(MARSHALL GROANS)

1102
00:52:20,942 --> 00:52:24,144
(GRUNTS, GROANS)

1103
00:52:40,494 --> 00:52:43,497
I don't need you
to be perfect.

1104
00:52:43,531 --> 00:52:46,968
I just need you to give it
everything you've got.

1105
00:52:47,001 --> 00:52:48,936
Can you do that
for me?

1106
00:52:48,970 --> 00:52:50,972
You can count
on me, Ryder.

1107
00:52:51,005 --> 00:52:52,740
(ENGINE WHIRS)

1108
00:52:54,909 --> 00:52:57,177
(ENGINE WHINES)

1109
00:52:58,311 --> 00:53:01,248
Is he okay?
Did you find Rhubarb?

1110
00:53:01,281 --> 00:53:03,216
No, not yet.

1111
00:53:03,250 --> 00:53:06,420
It's too dark
out there.
We can't see a thing.

1112
00:53:07,121 --> 00:53:08,856
But we're not giving up.

1113
00:53:08,890 --> 00:53:11,592
We'll start the search again
first thing in the morning.

1114
00:53:50,031 --> 00:53:52,432
Hey!
Where are you going?

1115
00:53:52,466 --> 00:53:54,401
I'm going
to find Rhubarb.

1116
00:53:54,434 --> 00:53:56,003
It's pitch black
out there.

1117
00:53:56,037 --> 00:53:58,873
There's no way you're gonna
find him in the dark.

1118
00:53:58,906 --> 00:54:02,409
I have to try. I can't just
sit around till morning.

1119
00:54:02,442 --> 00:54:04,579
The jungle's no joke
at night.

1120
00:54:04,612 --> 00:54:06,881
It's easy to get lost
out there.

1121
00:54:07,548 --> 00:54:09,584
I'm not giving up on him.

1122
00:54:15,322 --> 00:54:17,525
(INSECTS CHIRPING)

1123
00:54:20,528 --> 00:54:21,763
Rhubarb!

1124
00:54:24,732 --> 00:54:26,968
Rhubarb!
(DINOSAUR LOWS DISTANTLY)

1125
00:54:28,603 --> 00:54:30,872
Rhubarb?
(CREATURE SNARLS DISTANTLY)

1126
00:54:32,439 --> 00:54:34,474
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

1127
00:54:36,276 --> 00:54:37,344
(TWIG SNAPS)

1128
00:54:38,212 --> 00:54:40,648
Hello? Rhubarb?

1129
00:54:42,784 --> 00:54:44,619
(FAINT GROWL)

1130
00:54:44,652 --> 00:54:45,620
(WHIMPERS)

1131
00:54:46,053 --> 00:54:46,921
(YELPS)

1132
00:54:47,588 --> 00:54:49,456
(PANTING)

1133
00:54:54,494 --> 00:54:55,997
(ECHOING) Rhubarb?!

1134
00:54:56,564 --> 00:54:58,266
Rhubarb!

1135
00:54:58,298 --> 00:55:00,568
Where are you? (GRUNTS)

1136
00:55:01,636 --> 00:55:02,502
(GRUNTS)

1137
00:55:04,906 --> 00:55:06,406
Rhubarb!

1138
00:55:07,474 --> 00:55:08,976
(GRUNTS, YELPS)

1139
00:55:09,010 --> 00:55:10,511
(GRUNTS)

1140
00:55:11,279 --> 00:55:12,814
(COUGHS)

1141
00:55:13,313 --> 00:55:14,381
(GROANS)

1142
00:55:14,849 --> 00:55:16,083
I'm okay.

1143
00:55:17,718 --> 00:55:19,887
Yeah, I'm okay.

1144
00:55:22,223 --> 00:55:24,324
(INSECTS CHIRPING)

1145
00:55:27,595 --> 00:55:29,697
(SPRING CLICKS)
(GRUNTS, YELPS)

1146
00:55:29,730 --> 00:55:30,998
Whoa!

1147
00:55:31,032 --> 00:55:33,100
What's going on? (GRUNTS)

1148
00:55:33,134 --> 00:55:35,102
Get me out of here! (GRUNTS)

1149
00:55:35,136 --> 00:55:37,337
(GRUNTS) Help!

1150
00:55:37,905 --> 00:55:39,372
(CHITTERING)

1151
00:55:39,406 --> 00:55:40,842
(GRUNTS) Hmm.

1152
00:55:40,875 --> 00:55:43,077
HUMDINGER: Put them closer!
Pack it in there!

1153
00:55:43,110 --> 00:55:45,913
It's gonna be
the Fourth of July!

1154
00:55:45,947 --> 00:55:49,283
I think we've got
enough dynamite, boss.

1155
00:55:49,317 --> 00:55:51,986
It's enough
when I say it's enough!

1156
00:55:52,019 --> 00:55:54,021
Keep going! (CACKLES)

1157
00:55:54,055 --> 00:55:56,257
HARPER: Hey!
Guess what.

1158
00:55:56,290 --> 00:55:58,726
I caught
my first dinosaur.

1159
00:55:59,359 --> 00:56:00,393
Humdinger!

1160
00:56:00,427 --> 00:56:02,930
(SCOFFS)
That's not a dinosaur.

1161
00:56:02,964 --> 00:56:06,200
It's one of those dogs
from the PAW Patrol.

1162
00:56:06,234 --> 00:56:07,301
There are
so many of them,

1163
00:56:07,335 --> 00:56:09,237
I can never remember
their names.

1164
00:56:09,270 --> 00:56:11,305
Oh, oh, oh!
That one's Marshall!

1165
00:56:11,339 --> 00:56:13,507
He's my nephew's favorite!

1166
00:56:13,541 --> 00:56:14,976
(GASPS, SPUTTERS)

1167
00:56:15,009 --> 00:56:18,079
If I had known
you had a nephew
that liked the PAW Patrol,

1168
00:56:18,112 --> 00:56:20,014
I never would have hired you!

1169
00:56:20,047 --> 00:56:21,414
What are you
doing here?

1170
00:56:21,448 --> 00:56:23,284
Well,
we started out drilling,

1171
00:56:23,317 --> 00:56:25,152
but now we've moved on
to blasting.

1172
00:56:25,186 --> 00:56:26,921
Are you out of your mind?!

1173
00:56:26,954 --> 00:56:28,522
That's a dormant volcano!

1174
00:56:28,556 --> 00:56:29,924
If you set that thing off,

1175
00:56:29,957 --> 00:56:32,492
you're going to destroy
the island.

1176
00:56:32,526 --> 00:56:35,428
Well, I guess that's just
the cost of doing business.

1177
00:56:35,462 --> 00:56:38,633
Keep an eye on this one.
Those pups are slippery.

1178
00:56:38,666 --> 00:56:40,301
Don't let him
out of your sight.

1179
00:56:40,334 --> 00:56:43,070
Don't worry.
He's not going
anywhere.

1180
00:56:43,104 --> 00:56:44,705
(MARSHALL GRUNTS)

1181
00:56:44,739 --> 00:56:46,107
(GRUNTS)

1182
00:56:47,909 --> 00:56:49,143
(GRUNTS, SIGHS)

1183
00:56:50,311 --> 00:56:51,312
(PANTING)

1184
00:56:51,345 --> 00:56:52,713
You won't get away
with this.

1185
00:56:52,747 --> 00:56:54,315
(MOCKING) "You won't
get away with this."

1186
00:56:54,348 --> 00:56:56,050
(CHUCKLES)

1187
00:56:56,083 --> 00:56:59,620
I'm afraid it's you
who won't be
getting away.

1188
00:56:59,654 --> 00:57:00,487
(GROWLS)

1189
00:57:00,521 --> 00:57:02,156
ALISTAIR: That's all of it.

1190
00:57:02,189 --> 00:57:04,659
We're officially
out of dynamite.

1191
00:57:09,931 --> 00:57:11,565
Nice work, Marshall.

1192
00:57:11,599 --> 00:57:14,467
You didn't find Rhubarb,
you got yourself caught,

1193
00:57:14,501 --> 00:57:16,504
and now Humdinger's gonna
blow up the island

1194
00:57:16,537 --> 00:57:19,006
while you're stuck here
doing nothing.

1195
00:57:19,040 --> 00:57:21,876
So much for being the pup
who never gives up.

1196
00:57:22,810 --> 00:57:25,112
Who said anything
about giving up?

1197
00:57:26,113 --> 00:57:27,214
Rex?

1198
00:57:27,248 --> 00:57:28,582
What are you doing here?

1199
00:57:28,616 --> 00:57:31,451
I followed your trail.
And it's a good thing
I did.

1200
00:57:31,484 --> 00:57:32,853
Now let's get you
out of here.

1201
00:57:34,155 --> 00:57:35,455
What about her?

1202
00:57:37,658 --> 00:57:38,359
Heh.

1203
00:57:38,392 --> 00:57:39,827
I'll handle it.

1204
00:57:41,494 --> 00:57:43,197
(TRILLS, CLICKS)

1205
00:57:43,230 --> 00:57:46,067
(ALL CHITTERING)

1206
00:57:46,367 --> 00:57:47,234
(GRUNTS)

1207
00:57:48,002 --> 00:57:48,869
(GASPS)

1208
00:57:50,504 --> 00:57:51,739
What is this?

1209
00:57:51,772 --> 00:57:54,608
A bone-shaped cookie?
(RUSTLING)

1210
00:57:54,642 --> 00:57:57,878
(DINOSAURS CHITTERING)
(SCREAMS)

1211
00:57:57,912 --> 00:58:01,048
(LAUGHS) They love
those pup treats.

1212
00:58:01,082 --> 00:58:03,317
Humdinger's got
the whole volcano wired

1213
00:58:03,351 --> 00:58:04,452
with dynamite!

1214
00:58:04,484 --> 00:58:06,486
HUMDINGER: You might want
to plug your ears!

1215
00:58:06,520 --> 00:58:07,822
Wait, no, stop!

1216
00:58:07,855 --> 00:58:08,789
(GRUNTS)

1217
00:58:10,458 --> 00:58:13,427
(WHOOSHING, RUMBLING)

1218
00:58:13,461 --> 00:58:15,262
(BOTH YELP, GRUNT)

1219
00:58:15,296 --> 00:58:16,731
(GASPS)

1220
00:58:16,764 --> 00:58:17,832
(PANTS)

1221
00:58:17,865 --> 00:58:19,233
(GASPS)
(DIAMONDS CLINKING)

1222
00:58:25,172 --> 00:58:26,140
Whoo-hoo!

1223
00:58:26,173 --> 00:58:27,608
(CACKLES)

1224
00:58:28,242 --> 00:58:30,811
(CACKLES SHRILLY)

1225
00:58:31,278 --> 00:58:32,313
Whoa!

1226
00:58:32,346 --> 00:58:34,815
(CACKLES, YELPS)

1227
00:58:35,249 --> 00:58:37,351
(SNICKERS)

1228
00:58:37,385 --> 00:58:39,053
(GRUNTS, YELPS)

1229
00:58:41,489 --> 00:58:42,556
(WHOOPS)

1230
00:58:42,590 --> 00:58:45,926
Now that's what I call
having a blast!

1231
00:58:45,960 --> 00:58:47,361
(CACKLES)

1232
00:58:47,395 --> 00:58:48,929
(LOW RUMBLING)

1233
00:58:48,963 --> 00:58:50,364
(BOTH GASP)

1234
00:58:50,398 --> 00:58:52,133
The volcano!

1235
00:58:55,403 --> 00:58:57,838
We have to warn Ryder.
Come on!

1236
00:59:13,754 --> 00:59:15,089
REX: Ryder!
MARSHALL: Ryder!

1237
00:59:15,122 --> 00:59:17,625
Ryder!
Ryder!

1238
00:59:17,658 --> 00:59:20,194
Marshall! Rex!
Where were you?

1239
00:59:20,227 --> 00:59:21,328
Humdinger's here!

1240
00:59:21,362 --> 00:59:22,730
Humdinger?!

1241
00:59:22,763 --> 00:59:25,199
He just set off
a thousand sticks of dynamite

1242
00:59:25,232 --> 00:59:26,500
on the side of the volcano.

1243
00:59:26,535 --> 00:59:28,335
(DISTANT BOOM)
(PUPS WINCE)

1244
00:59:29,336 --> 00:59:32,106
(RUMBLES, WHOOSHES)

1245
00:59:33,207 --> 00:59:34,308
(PANTING)
Whoa!

1246
00:59:34,341 --> 00:59:35,976
What on earth?
Oh, no.

1247
00:59:36,010 --> 00:59:38,813
(LAVA BOMBS WHISTLING,
BOOMING)

1248
00:59:39,647 --> 00:59:42,283
Rhubarb's still out there!
(WHOOSHING)

1249
00:59:42,316 --> 00:59:44,752
RYDER: Look out!
(PUPS YELP)

1250
00:59:44,785 --> 00:59:48,089
We've got to get
all the people
and the dinosaurs to safety.

1251
00:59:48,122 --> 00:59:49,790
We're on it!

1252
00:59:49,824 --> 00:59:52,827
What about Rhubarb?
Don't worry. I'll find him.

1253
00:59:52,860 --> 00:59:54,895
Then you're
gonna need this.

1254
00:59:59,066 --> 01:00:01,936
My truck!
Meet us
at the caverns.

1255
01:00:03,304 --> 01:00:05,372
(ENGINE REVS)

1256
01:00:05,406 --> 01:00:07,975
I'm fired up!
(ENGINE RUMBLES)

1257
01:00:12,113 --> 01:00:13,447
(WHISTLES)

1258
01:00:13,481 --> 01:00:14,583
Where's Timmy?

1259
01:00:14,615 --> 01:00:15,983
When I was fixing
Marshall's truck,

1260
01:00:16,016 --> 01:00:18,619
I made a few upgrades
to your ride, too.

1261
01:00:18,652 --> 01:00:19,820
(THUDS)

1262
01:00:22,189 --> 01:00:24,825
(ROARS)

1263
01:00:25,926 --> 01:00:26,894
Whoa!

1264
01:00:26,927 --> 01:00:30,331
Let's roll out!
We've got an island to save.

1265
01:00:35,136 --> 01:00:37,138
(ENGINE FADES DISTANTLY)

1266
01:00:38,439 --> 01:00:41,075
(SCIENTISTS SCREAMING)

1267
01:00:41,108 --> 01:00:44,945
This job is
much more dangerous
than I thought it would be.

1268
01:00:44,979 --> 01:00:46,046
BOTH: Whoa!

1269
01:00:53,120 --> 01:00:55,422
We've got to get
everyone to the caverns.

1270
01:00:55,456 --> 01:00:57,526
It's the only place
we'll be safe.

1271
01:00:57,559 --> 01:00:59,293
Come on!
Let's move it, people!

1272
01:00:59,326 --> 01:01:01,563
(DINOSAURS CHITTER)
(SCIENTISTS MURMURING)

1273
01:01:01,596 --> 01:01:03,664
Everybody on!

1274
01:01:03,697 --> 01:01:06,500
(SCIENTISTS SHOUTING)
(WHOOSHES, BOOMS)

1275
01:01:06,535 --> 01:01:09,003
(ENGINE REVS)
Okay, go, go!

1276
01:01:09,036 --> 01:01:11,071
SCIENTIST: Wait up!
Wait up!

1277
01:01:16,277 --> 01:01:17,344
(ALISTAIR GRUNTS, SIGHS)

1278
01:01:18,312 --> 01:01:20,114
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1279
01:01:21,248 --> 01:01:22,082
HUMDINGER: Over here!

1280
01:01:22,116 --> 01:01:24,185
Help me get the big one.
(CHUCKLES)

1281
01:01:24,218 --> 01:01:27,121
The bigger they are,
the more they're worth!

1282
01:01:27,154 --> 01:01:29,857
The truck's full
of diamonds.
We're already rich.

1283
01:01:29,890 --> 01:01:31,458
Let's get out
of here, man!

1284
01:01:31,492 --> 01:01:33,961
But look at the size
of this thing!

1285
01:01:33,994 --> 01:01:37,198
You think there's
a lesson here about
not being too greedy?

1286
01:01:37,731 --> 01:01:39,733
No, I don't.

1287
01:01:39,767 --> 01:01:41,268
Now get over here
and lift!

1288
01:01:42,336 --> 01:01:45,005
(ALL STRAINING)

1289
01:01:45,039 --> 01:01:48,275
Come on, you weaklings,
lift with your backs.

1290
01:01:48,309 --> 01:01:50,044
(ALL STRAIN)

1291
01:01:51,412 --> 01:01:53,515
(FRANTIC YOWLS)
(HONKING)

1292
01:01:53,548 --> 01:01:55,115
(GROANS)
(GASPS)

1293
01:01:55,149 --> 01:01:55,849
(GASPS)

1294
01:01:55,883 --> 01:01:57,251
(GRUNTS, STRAINS)

1295
01:01:57,284 --> 01:01:59,019
Lift!

1296
01:01:59,053 --> 01:02:01,155
Uh, we should really
get out of here.

1297
01:02:01,188 --> 01:02:04,491
No! I am not leaving
this diamond.

1298
01:02:05,226 --> 01:02:07,127
(STRAINS)

1299
01:02:07,562 --> 01:02:08,462
Huh?

1300
01:02:08,495 --> 01:02:11,065
Oh! (FRANTIC YELPING)

1301
01:02:11,098 --> 01:02:14,768
(ALL SCREAMING)

1302
01:02:16,503 --> 01:02:19,406
(LAVA BUBBLING)

1303
01:02:19,440 --> 01:02:21,610
No!

1304
01:02:21,643 --> 01:02:24,011
(KITTIES SOB)

1305
01:02:27,582 --> 01:02:28,782
(SQUAWKS)

1306
01:02:28,816 --> 01:02:30,284
GENE: Hey, hey, hey!
(SMACKING)
(CHITTERS)

1307
01:02:30,317 --> 01:02:31,519
Come on,
little buddy.

1308
01:02:31,553 --> 01:02:32,486
Come on.
(SQUEALS)

1309
01:02:32,520 --> 01:02:34,154
We got to get you
out of here.

1310
01:02:34,188 --> 01:02:35,923
(BOOM)

1311
01:02:38,392 --> 01:02:40,160
Come on now. Come on.
(DINOSAUR CHITTERS)

1312
01:02:40,194 --> 01:02:41,295
(GASPS)
Get down from that tree.

1313
01:02:41,328 --> 01:02:42,697
No, no, no, no, no!
Get up in the tree!

1314
01:02:42,731 --> 01:02:43,797
Get up in the tree!

1315
01:02:46,033 --> 01:02:47,669
(SCIENTISTS PANTING)
(SQUEALS FEARFULLY)

1316
01:02:47,702 --> 01:02:49,436
(PANTING)

1317
01:02:49,470 --> 01:02:50,639
(SCREAMS)

1318
01:02:50,672 --> 01:02:52,873
(SCIENTISTS
AND DINOSAUR SCREAM)

1319
01:02:52,906 --> 01:02:55,409
(SCIENTISTS SCREAM)

1320
01:02:56,477 --> 01:02:59,480
(CHITTERING, SQUEALING)

1321
01:03:01,048 --> 01:03:03,551
All right, Timmy,
I'm gonna grab them.

1322
01:03:03,585 --> 01:03:05,919
Come on, little guys.
Hop on.

1323
01:03:05,953 --> 01:03:07,888
(DINOSAURS CHITTER)

1324
01:03:07,921 --> 01:03:09,323
(MACHINERY WHIRS)

1325
01:03:09,724 --> 01:03:11,025
(HOWLS)

1326
01:03:11,058 --> 01:03:13,561
(DINOSAURS SQUEALING)

1327
01:03:13,595 --> 01:03:15,429
I'm happy to give you a ride,

1328
01:03:15,462 --> 01:03:16,564
but you have to promise

1329
01:03:16,598 --> 01:03:19,199
not to steal
any more of my pup treats.

1330
01:03:19,233 --> 01:03:20,467
(CHITTERS)

1331
01:03:20,501 --> 01:03:22,870
Oh, come on!
(DINOSAURS GIGGLE)

1332
01:03:26,373 --> 01:03:28,510
(DEVICE RINGS, BEEPS)

1333
01:03:28,543 --> 01:03:31,780
<i>This is Gene and Heidi.</i>
<i>We're stuck in a mudslide.</i>

1334
01:03:31,812 --> 01:03:34,181
<i>We need an evac... ASAP!</i>

1335
01:03:34,214 --> 01:03:35,149
Copy that, Gene.

1336
01:03:35,182 --> 01:03:37,117
I've got eyes
on your location.

1337
01:03:39,654 --> 01:03:40,921
(WHOOSH)

1338
01:03:41,488 --> 01:03:42,823
(DISTANT BOOM)

1339
01:03:42,856 --> 01:03:43,758
(GASPS)

1340
01:03:43,792 --> 01:03:45,727
(JET RATTLING)
(ALERTS BEEPING)

1341
01:03:45,760 --> 01:03:47,027
Okay, change of plan.

1342
01:03:47,061 --> 01:03:49,997
I can't fly.
There's too much ash
in the air.

1343
01:03:50,030 --> 01:03:52,667
We're gonna have to do
this rescue from the ground.

1344
01:03:52,701 --> 01:03:54,569
(WHIRRING)

1345
01:03:56,671 --> 01:03:57,539
(GRUNTS)

1346
01:03:59,173 --> 01:04:01,509
Chase, I'm gonna need backup.

1347
01:04:01,543 --> 01:04:03,077
CHASE: <i>Already on my way.</i>

1348
01:04:04,713 --> 01:04:05,580
(WHOOSHES)

1349
01:04:06,313 --> 01:04:07,515
(ENGINE ROARS)

1350
01:04:10,284 --> 01:04:12,721
(BEEPS)
Marshall, this is Ryder.

1351
01:04:12,754 --> 01:04:14,556
Any sign of Rhubarb?

1352
01:04:14,589 --> 01:04:15,690
MARSHALL: <i>Not yet.</i>

1353
01:04:15,724 --> 01:04:18,258
But I'm not coming in
until I find him.

1354
01:04:19,527 --> 01:04:20,928
(LAVA BOMB WHISTLES)

1355
01:04:22,396 --> 01:04:24,699
(ENGINE ROARS)

1356
01:04:24,733 --> 01:04:25,834
There they are!

1357
01:04:25,866 --> 01:04:27,901
HEIDI: Over here!
GENE: Help!

1358
01:04:27,935 --> 01:04:30,070
SKYE: Hang on!
We're coming!

1359
01:04:30,104 --> 01:04:32,072
Skye, I'm gonna fire
my grappling hook

1360
01:04:32,106 --> 01:04:33,608
across to you.
(BEEPS)

1361
01:04:33,641 --> 01:04:34,676
SKYE: Ready when you are.

1362
01:04:34,709 --> 01:04:35,876
Fire!
(CHIMES)

1363
01:04:38,345 --> 01:04:39,313
Nice shot.

1364
01:04:39,748 --> 01:04:41,081
CHASE: Bullseye!

1365
01:04:41,949 --> 01:04:43,618
CHASE: Get on!
(GENE GRUNTS)

1366
01:04:43,651 --> 01:04:45,653
(GROANS) Got it!
Whoa.

1367
01:04:45,687 --> 01:04:47,689
(GASPING)
And up we go!

1368
01:04:47,722 --> 01:04:48,922
(BOTH GRUNT)

1369
01:04:50,090 --> 01:04:52,259
(SCREAMS)
(GRUNTS)

1370
01:04:52,292 --> 01:04:55,162
(SQUEALS, CHITTERS)
(GASPS)

1371
01:04:55,195 --> 01:04:57,599
(SCIENTISTS YELLING)
SKYE: Climb toward me!

1372
01:04:57,632 --> 01:04:58,600
(BOTH GRUNT)

1373
01:04:58,633 --> 01:05:00,968
Climb, climb,
climb!

1374
01:05:01,001 --> 01:05:02,871
Uh-oh. Hill!

1375
01:05:02,903 --> 01:05:04,238
(BOTH GRUNT)

1376
01:05:04,271 --> 01:05:07,441
Oh-- Whoa!
(HEIDI YELPS)

1377
01:05:07,474 --> 01:05:10,077
(BOTH GROANING)

1378
01:05:10,110 --> 01:05:12,747
Okay, let's try that again.

1379
01:05:12,781 --> 01:05:14,381
(GRUNTS, GASPS)

1380
01:05:16,383 --> 01:05:20,187
If this rope hits that rock,
it's going to cut it in half!

1381
01:05:20,220 --> 01:05:23,525
Okay, I'm climbing,
I'm climbing!

1382
01:05:23,558 --> 01:05:25,426
(PANTING)

1383
01:05:25,860 --> 01:05:28,095
(BOTH SCREAM)

1384
01:05:28,128 --> 01:05:29,963
You're
almost there!
Grab on!

1385
01:05:29,997 --> 01:05:33,701
Oh, No, no, no, no, no!
(SCREAMS)

1386
01:05:33,735 --> 01:05:35,169
BOTH: Whoa!

1387
01:05:35,202 --> 01:05:37,772
This is getting ridiculous!

1388
01:05:37,806 --> 01:05:39,173
It's now or never.

1389
01:05:41,074 --> 01:05:43,343
Time to take the high road.
(GRUNTS)

1390
01:05:46,113 --> 01:05:48,650
(GRUNTS)
(ENGINE REVS, TIRES SQUEAL)

1391
01:05:49,918 --> 01:05:53,454
(ALL SCREAMING)

1392
01:05:55,523 --> 01:05:56,925
(GASPS)
(GRUNTS)

1393
01:05:56,957 --> 01:05:58,158
SKYE: Got them!

1394
01:05:58,192 --> 01:06:00,327
(LAUGHS)
(DINOSAUR WHOOPS)

1395
01:06:00,360 --> 01:06:01,061
CHASE: Yeah!

1396
01:06:01,094 --> 01:06:03,163
Nice catch, Skye!

1397
01:06:03,197 --> 01:06:05,567
Hang on.
(ENGINE ROARS)

1398
01:06:13,641 --> 01:06:15,677
Rhubarb! Rhubarb!

1399
01:06:17,912 --> 01:06:19,079
Rhubarb!

1400
01:06:19,980 --> 01:06:21,215
Rhubarb!

1401
01:06:25,452 --> 01:06:26,888
Rhubarb?

1402
01:06:26,921 --> 01:06:28,523
Rhubarb, where are you?

1403
01:06:28,556 --> 01:06:31,058
Come on, buddy,
we've got to get out of here!

1404
01:06:31,091 --> 01:06:33,126
(LEAVES RUSTLE)

1405
01:06:33,160 --> 01:06:35,195
(RUSTLING CONTINUES)

1406
01:06:35,229 --> 01:06:36,296
Rhubarb!

1407
01:06:38,265 --> 01:06:41,168
Well, look who it is.

1408
01:06:41,201 --> 01:06:43,070
(YELPS) Humdinger!
(HUMDINGER CACKLES)

1409
01:06:43,103 --> 01:06:44,404
Look what
you've done!

1410
01:06:44,438 --> 01:06:47,842
Oh, no.
You're not going
to pin this on me.

1411
01:06:47,876 --> 01:06:50,912
You and the PAW Patrol
love to blame
old Humdinger

1412
01:06:50,945 --> 01:06:52,246
for everything!

1413
01:06:52,279 --> 01:06:54,314
Where are the rest
of your friends now,

1414
01:06:54,348 --> 01:06:56,885
little puppy dog?
(GRUNTS)

1415
01:06:56,918 --> 01:06:59,286
It's just you and me.

1416
01:06:59,319 --> 01:07:00,354
(WHIMPERS)

1417
01:07:06,728 --> 01:07:08,328
(ROARS)

1418
01:07:08,362 --> 01:07:10,430
(SCREAMS)

1419
01:07:11,431 --> 01:07:13,568
Yeah, Rhubarb!

1420
01:07:14,468 --> 01:07:15,202
(GASPS)

1421
01:07:15,235 --> 01:07:18,238
(ROARS)
(SQUEALS)

1422
01:07:18,272 --> 01:07:21,709
(SCREAMING SHRILLY)

1423
01:07:22,442 --> 01:07:24,378
Now that's a roar!

1424
01:07:25,947 --> 01:07:29,383
(LOWS)
(PAW PATROL PANTING)

1425
01:07:29,416 --> 01:07:33,487
Everybody, get under cover!
We'll be safe in the cavern.

1426
01:07:33,521 --> 01:07:35,155
(INDISTINCT YELLING)

1427
01:07:35,188 --> 01:07:37,825
(DINOSAURS LOWING)

1428
01:07:38,793 --> 01:07:40,427
SCIENTIST:
Come on, come on!

1429
01:07:43,031 --> 01:07:46,534
Is that the last of the dinos?
Is everybody safe?

1430
01:07:46,568 --> 01:07:50,137
No. Marshall and Rhubarb
are still out there.

1431
01:07:56,343 --> 01:07:58,445
Don't worry.
We'll be out of this soon.

1432
01:07:58,478 --> 01:08:00,782
We're gonna take cover
in the cavern.

1433
01:08:02,617 --> 01:08:04,384
Let's clear a path!

1434
01:08:06,153 --> 01:08:09,222
<i>♪ We're going places</i>
<i>We've never been</i>

1435
01:08:09,256 --> 01:08:12,125
<i>♪ Off to the races</i>
<i>We about to win</i>

1436
01:08:12,159 --> 01:08:15,329
<i>♪ I feel amazing</i>
<i>Ten out of ten</i>

1437
01:08:15,362 --> 01:08:16,898
<i>♪ Let's go</i>
(BEEPING)

1438
01:08:16,931 --> 01:08:18,766
<i>♪ Let's go</i>
Ooh...

1439
01:08:18,800 --> 01:08:21,501
<i>♪ Hands up if you're ready</i>

1440
01:08:21,536 --> 01:08:24,338
<i>♪ Hold up, keep it steady</i>
Rhubarb, what are you doing?

1441
01:08:24,371 --> 01:08:27,575
<i>♪ Go off like confetti</i>

1442
01:08:27,609 --> 01:08:30,177
<i>♪ Hold on tight</i>

1443
01:08:30,210 --> 01:08:33,313
<i>♪ You better work</i>
<i>Ooh-ooh</i>

1444
01:08:33,347 --> 01:08:36,116
<i>♪ You better work</i>
<i>Ooh-ooh</i>

1445
01:08:36,149 --> 01:08:38,653
<i>♪ Let's get to work</i>
Yeah, Rhubarb!

1446
01:08:38,686 --> 01:08:41,355
Nice moves! You're a natural!
(WHIRRING)

1447
01:08:41,388 --> 01:08:43,725
<i>♪ Work, work, work, work ♪</i>
(GROANS)

1448
01:08:50,598 --> 01:08:52,165
(GASPS, GRUNTS)

1449
01:08:57,237 --> 01:08:58,438
RYDER: Marshall!

1450
01:08:58,906 --> 01:09:00,041
Marshall!

1451
01:09:00,074 --> 01:09:02,010
(OVERLAPPING SHOUTS)

1452
01:09:02,043 --> 01:09:03,077
We're trapped!

1453
01:09:03,111 --> 01:09:05,479
Everybody, stand back!

1454
01:09:14,722 --> 01:09:17,058
(LAVA BUBBLES, HISSES)

1455
01:09:17,091 --> 01:09:20,695
It's not working!
There's not enough water!

1456
01:09:28,335 --> 01:09:31,371
If I can get up that cliff
and release that water,

1457
01:09:31,405 --> 01:09:33,473
we might stand a chance.

1458
01:09:36,077 --> 01:09:37,945
Marshall,
what are you doing?

1459
01:09:38,813 --> 01:09:39,714
On my signal,

1460
01:09:39,747 --> 01:09:41,883
point the water cannons
straight down.

1461
01:09:41,916 --> 01:09:43,383
(BABBLES)

1462
01:09:43,918 --> 01:09:44,852
Ready...

1463
01:09:46,988 --> 01:09:48,221
aim...

1464
01:09:50,158 --> 01:09:51,291
fire!

1465
01:09:59,133 --> 01:10:01,301
(ENGINE WHIRS)

1466
01:10:05,238 --> 01:10:07,542
He's trying to cross it.

1467
01:10:09,877 --> 01:10:11,112
It's working!

1468
01:10:11,145 --> 01:10:14,314
(SIZZLING, BUBBLING)

1469
01:10:15,650 --> 01:10:17,317
Marshall, hurry!

1470
01:10:17,719 --> 01:10:18,586
Huh?

1471
01:10:18,619 --> 01:10:21,522
(SIZZLING, BUBBLING)
(GASPS, SQUEAKS)

1472
01:10:22,957 --> 01:10:24,424
(RUMBLES)
(GRUNTS)

1473
01:10:25,126 --> 01:10:27,695
No, no!
Come on, come on!

1474
01:10:28,196 --> 01:10:29,964
No, no! (YELPS)

1475
01:10:29,997 --> 01:10:31,666
(CROWD GASPS)
(MARSHALL YELPS)

1476
01:10:31,699 --> 01:10:32,934
Marshall!

1477
01:10:32,967 --> 01:10:34,702
Rhubarb, get out of there!

1478
01:10:40,108 --> 01:10:42,110
We're gonna have to jump.

1479
01:10:42,143 --> 01:10:44,178
Three, two,

1480
01:10:44,212 --> 01:10:45,813
one, now!
(GROWLS)

1481
01:10:47,280 --> 01:10:49,316
(MARSHALL GRUNTING)

1482
01:10:49,751 --> 01:10:52,352
(YELPS, YELLS)

1483
01:10:54,421 --> 01:10:56,124
(CROWD CHEERS)
(PUPS HOWL)

1484
01:10:56,157 --> 01:10:57,491
He did it!

1485
